-- Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376) -- THE SEAT LAYER for Part 5, Part 8 and Schedules 6 to 9, 11 and 12 (piece uc4).
-- The seat is a person who claims or receives Universal Credit, alone or as one of a couple. Every question below is exported, takes
-- plain facts that person can state, and calls the layer-1 rules in the uc4-*.l4 modules without restating them.
-- How the questions are built:
--   * The Secretary of State's judgments ("is satisfied that", "considers") are yes-or-no inputs that the person states or reads from a
--     decision letter; the layer never decides them.
--   * A fact that may not exist (a date, an amount, a finding) is a MAYBE input: leave it blank. A question the text does not answer
--     for the facts given returns NOTHING (a MAYBE result) or a named constructor, never FALSE or 0.
--   * The Part 5 descriptors, the benefits the person gets and the earlier failures are asked as lists or as one earlier failure.
--   * Some facts are asked once for a whole group of activities or of limbs (see the comment above each question).
-- The worked cases are in uc4-cases-seat.l4; the NOTES.md section "Seat" lists the questions.

§ `Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (Parts 5 and 8) -- the claimant's questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Whether I have limited capability for work or for work-related activity`

-- Regulation 39(2) to (5) with Schedule 6. "Limited capability for work" is the status that moves a claimant out of the work search
-- requirement: the person is assessed against 17 activities, each with descriptors worth points, and needs 15 points. The person
-- states, for each activity, which descriptors fit them (more than one may; the highest counts). Two further facts say whether each
-- group of limitations comes from a specific bodily disease or disablement, or from medical treatment for one (physical activities
-- 1 to 10), or from a specific mental illness or disablement, or from treatment for one (mental activities 11 to 17); the person
-- states each once, for the whole group.
@export Do I have limited capability for work on the points I score for my physical and mental limitations (reg 39(2) to (5), Schedule 6)?
GIVEN `I have a specific bodily or mental disease or disablement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have some specific disease, or some bodily or mental disablement?
      `my physical limitations arise from a bodily disease or disablement, or from treatment for one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your physical limitations (activities 1 to 10) arise from a specific bodily disease or disablement, or directly from treatment by a registered doctor for a specific physical disease or disablement?
      `my mental limitations arise from a mental illness or disablement, or from treatment for one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your mental limitations (activities 11 to 17) arise from a specific mental illness or disablement, or directly from treatment by a registered doctor for a specific mental illness or disablement?
      `my activity 1 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 1 descriptor` @desc Activity 1, mobilising (walking about, with any stick, wheelchair or other aid you normally use or could reasonably use): which of the descriptors 1(a) to 1(e) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 2 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 2 descriptor` @desc Activity 2, standing and sitting: which of the descriptors 2(a) to 2(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 3 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 3 descriptor` @desc Activity 3, reaching: which of the descriptors 3(a) to 3(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 4 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 4 descriptor` @desc Activity 4, picking up and moving things with your upper body and arms: which of the descriptors 4(a) to 4(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 5 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 5 descriptor` @desc Activity 5, manual dexterity (using your hands): which of the descriptors 5(a) to 5(e) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 6 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 6 descriptor` @desc Activity 6, making yourself understood by speaking, writing, typing or other means, without help from another person: which of the descriptors 6(a) to 6(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 7 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 7 descriptor` @desc Activity 7, understanding communication by verbal means, non-verbal means or both, using any aid you normally use or could reasonably use: which of the descriptors 7(a) to 7(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 8 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 8 descriptor` @desc Activity 8, navigating and keeping yourself safe, using any guide dog or other aid you normally use or could reasonably use: which of the descriptors 8(a) to 8(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 9 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 9 descriptor` @desc Activity 9, loss of control of your bowel or bladder while conscious (other than bed-wetting): which of the descriptors 9(a) to 9(c) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 10 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 10 descriptor` @desc Activity 10, consciousness during waking moments: which of the descriptors 10(a) to 10(c) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 11 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 11 descriptor` @desc Activity 11, learning tasks: which of the descriptors 11(a) to 11(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 12 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 12 descriptor` @desc Activity 12, awareness of everyday hazards, such as boiling water or sharp objects: which of the descriptors 12(a) to 12(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 13 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 13 descriptor` @desc Activity 13, initiating and completing personal action (planning, organising, problem solving, prioritising or switching tasks): which of the descriptors 13(a) to 13(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 14 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 14 descriptor` @desc Activity 14, coping with change: which of the descriptors 14(a) to 14(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 15 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 15 descriptor` @desc Activity 15, getting about: which of the descriptors 15(a) to 15(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 16 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 16 descriptor` @desc Activity 16, coping with social engagement, because of a cognitive impairment or mental disorder: which of the descriptors 16(a) to 16(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 17 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 17 descriptor` @desc Activity 17, appropriateness of behaviour with other people, because of a cognitive impairment or mental disorder: which of the descriptors 17(a) to 17(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have limited capability for work on the points I score` IF
    `reg 39(2) to (5) — limited capability for work on the basis of an assessment under this Part` `I have a specific bodily or mental disease or disablement` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my physical causes` MEANS
            IF `my physical limitations arise from a bodily disease or disablement, or from treatment for one`
            THEN LIST `a specific bodily disease or disablement`, `treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement`
            ELSE EMPTY
        `my mental causes` MEANS
            IF `my mental limitations arise from a mental illness or disablement, or from treatment for one`
            THEN LIST `a specific mental illness or disablement`, `treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement`
            ELSE EMPTY
        `my facts` MEANS `Sch 6 claimant facts` WITH
            `activity 1: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 1 descriptors`
            `activity 1: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 2: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 2 descriptors`
            `activity 2: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 3: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 3 descriptors`
            `activity 3: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 4: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 4 descriptors`
            `activity 4: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 5: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 5 descriptors`
            `activity 5: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 6: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 6 descriptors`
            `activity 6: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 7: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 7 descriptors`
            `activity 7: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 8: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 8 descriptors`
            `activity 8: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 9: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 9 descriptors`
            `activity 9: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 10: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 10 descriptors`
            `activity 10: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 11: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 11 descriptors`
            `activity 11: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`
            `activity 12: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 12 descriptors`
            `activity 12: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`
            `activity 13: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 13 descriptors`
            `activity 13: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`
            `activity 14: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 14 descriptors`
            `activity 14: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`
            `activity 15: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 15 descriptors`
            `activity 15: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`
            `activity 16: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 16 descriptors`
            `activity 16: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`
            `activity 17: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 17 descriptors`
            `activity 17: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`

-- Regulation 39(3) with Schedule 6: the points are added up over Part 1 (activities 1 to 10) and Part 2 (activities 11 to 17), and
-- 15 points in either Part, or 15 in the two together, give limited capability for work. This question gives the two totals added.
@export How many points do I score in all for my physical and mental limitations (reg 39(3), Schedule 6)?
GIVEN `my physical limitations arise from a bodily disease or disablement, or from treatment for one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your physical limitations (activities 1 to 10) arise from a specific bodily disease or disablement, or directly from treatment by a registered doctor for a specific physical disease or disablement?
      `my mental limitations arise from a mental illness or disablement, or from treatment for one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your mental limitations (activities 11 to 17) arise from a specific mental illness or disablement, or directly from treatment by a registered doctor for a specific mental illness or disablement?
      `my activity 1 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 1 descriptor` @desc Activity 1, mobilising (walking about, with any stick, wheelchair or other aid you normally use or could reasonably use): which of the descriptors 1(a) to 1(e) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 2 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 2 descriptor` @desc Activity 2, standing and sitting: which of the descriptors 2(a) to 2(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 3 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 3 descriptor` @desc Activity 3, reaching: which of the descriptors 3(a) to 3(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 4 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 4 descriptor` @desc Activity 4, picking up and moving things with your upper body and arms: which of the descriptors 4(a) to 4(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 5 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 5 descriptor` @desc Activity 5, manual dexterity (using your hands): which of the descriptors 5(a) to 5(e) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 6 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 6 descriptor` @desc Activity 6, making yourself understood by speaking, writing, typing or other means, without help from another person: which of the descriptors 6(a) to 6(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 7 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 7 descriptor` @desc Activity 7, understanding communication by verbal means, non-verbal means or both, using any aid you normally use or could reasonably use: which of the descriptors 7(a) to 7(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 8 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 8 descriptor` @desc Activity 8, navigating and keeping yourself safe, using any guide dog or other aid you normally use or could reasonably use: which of the descriptors 8(a) to 8(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 9 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 9 descriptor` @desc Activity 9, loss of control of your bowel or bladder while conscious (other than bed-wetting): which of the descriptors 9(a) to 9(c) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 10 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 10 descriptor` @desc Activity 10, consciousness during waking moments: which of the descriptors 10(a) to 10(c) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 11 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 11 descriptor` @desc Activity 11, learning tasks: which of the descriptors 11(a) to 11(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 12 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 12 descriptor` @desc Activity 12, awareness of everyday hazards, such as boiling water or sharp objects: which of the descriptors 12(a) to 12(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 13 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 13 descriptor` @desc Activity 13, initiating and completing personal action (planning, organising, problem solving, prioritising or switching tasks): which of the descriptors 13(a) to 13(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 14 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 14 descriptor` @desc Activity 14, coping with change: which of the descriptors 14(a) to 14(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 15 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 15 descriptor` @desc Activity 15, getting about: which of the descriptors 15(a) to 15(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 16 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 16 descriptor` @desc Activity 16, coping with social engagement, because of a cognitive impairment or mental disorder: which of the descriptors 16(a) to 16(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my activity 17 descriptors` IS A LIST OF `Sch 6 activity 17 descriptor` @desc Activity 17, appropriateness of behaviour with other people, because of a cognitive impairment or mental disorder: which of the descriptors 17(a) to 17(d) apply to you? Choose all that apply, or none.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many points do I score in all` IS
    `reg 39(3) — the points scored in Part 1 of Schedule 6` `my facts` PLUS `reg 39(3) — the points scored in Part 2 of Schedule 6` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my physical causes` MEANS
            IF `my physical limitations arise from a bodily disease or disablement, or from treatment for one`
            THEN LIST `a specific bodily disease or disablement`, `treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement`
            ELSE EMPTY
        `my mental causes` MEANS
            IF `my mental limitations arise from a mental illness or disablement, or from treatment for one`
            THEN LIST `a specific mental illness or disablement`, `treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement`
            ELSE EMPTY
        `my facts` MEANS `Sch 6 claimant facts` WITH
            `activity 1: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 1 descriptors`
            `activity 1: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 2: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 2 descriptors`
            `activity 2: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 3: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 3 descriptors`
            `activity 3: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 4: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 4 descriptors`
            `activity 4: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 5: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 5 descriptors`
            `activity 5: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 6: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 6 descriptors`
            `activity 6: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 7: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 7 descriptors`
            `activity 7: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 8: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 8 descriptors`
            `activity 8: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 9: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 9 descriptors`
            `activity 9: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 10: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 10 descriptors`
            `activity 10: what the incapability arises from` IS `my physical causes`
            `activity 11: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 11 descriptors`
            `activity 11: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`
            `activity 12: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 12 descriptors`
            `activity 12: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`
            `activity 13: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 13 descriptors`
            `activity 13: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`
            `activity 14: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 14 descriptors`
            `activity 14: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`
            `activity 15: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 15 descriptors`
            `activity 15: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`
            `activity 16: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 16 descriptors`
            `activity 16: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`
            `activity 17: descriptors that apply` IS `my activity 17 descriptors`
            `activity 17: what the incapability arises from` IS `my mental causes`

-- Regulation 39(6) and (7) with Schedule 8. A claimant in one of the Schedule 8 circumstances is treated as having limited capability
-- for work whatever the assessment would find, unless the assessment under this Part has already found it (regulation 39(1) and (7)).
@export Am I treated as having limited capability for work because of my treatment, infection, risk or age (reg 39(6) and (7), Schedule 8)?
GIVEN `my assessment under this Part has found limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an assessment of your capability for work (the work capability assessment) found that you have limited capability for work?
      `I receive regular weekly haemodialysis for chronic renal failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive regular weekly treatment by haemodialysis for chronic renal failure?
      `I receive plasmapheresis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive treatment by plasmapheresis?
      `I receive regular weekly total parenteral nutrition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive regular weekly treatment by total parenteral nutrition for gross impairment of enteric function?
      `I am recovering from one of those treatments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you recovering from one of those forms of treatment?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied I should be treated as having limited capability for work after that treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that you should be treated as having limited capability for work while you recover from that treatment?
      `I am a patient in a hospital or similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undergoing medical or other treatment as a patient in a hospital or similar institution?
      `I attend a residential programme of rehabilitation for drug or alcohol dependency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you attending a residential programme of rehabilitation for the treatment of drug or alcohol dependency?
      `I have been advised to stay 24 hours or more after treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been advised to stay for 24 hours or longer after medical or other treatment?
      `the person who advised me is a registered medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that advice given by a registered medical practitioner?
      `the person who advised me is a registered nurse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that advice given by a registered nurse?
      `the person who advised me is an occupational therapist or physiotherapist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that advice given by an occupational therapist or physiotherapist?
      `the person who advised me is registered with a body under section 60 of the Health Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that occupational therapist or physiotherapist registered with a regulatory body established by Order in Council under section 60 of the Health Act 1999?
      `I am recovering from treatment as a hospital patient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you recovering from such hospital treatment?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied I should be treated as having limited capability for work after hospital treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that you should be treated as having limited capability for work while you recover from that hospital treatment?
      `the nation I live in` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc Do you live in England, Wales or Scotland?
      `I am excluded or abstain from work under a written request or notice made under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you excluded, or do you abstain, from work under a written request or notice lawfully made or given under an enactment?
      `I am otherwise prevented from working under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you otherwise prevented from working under an enactment?
      `it is known or suspected that I am infected or contaminated, or have been in contact with a case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it known or reasonably suspected that you are infected or contaminated, or have been in contact with a case of infection or contamination?
      `the infection or contamination is within section 45A(3) of the Public Health (Control of Disease) Act 1984` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an incidence or spread of infection or contamination that section 45A(3) of the Public Health (Control of Disease) Act 1984 covers, for which regulations are made under Part 2A of that Act?
      `it is tuberculosis or an infectious disease of the Public Health (Aircraft) or (Ships) Regulations 1979` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it tuberculosis, or an infectious disease to which regulation 9 of the Public Health (Aircraft) Regulations 1979 or regulation 10 of the Public Health (Ships) Regulations 1979 applies?
      `it is an infectious disease within section 1(5) of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an infectious disease within section 1(5) of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008, or exposure to an organism causing that disease?
      `it is a contamination within section 1(5) of that Scottish Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it contamination within section 1(5) of that Act, or exposure to a contaminant?
      `sections 56 to 58 of the Scottish Act on compensation apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do sections 56 to 58 of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008 (compensation) apply to it?
      `I suffer from a specific illness, disease or disablement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a specific illness, disease or disablement?
      `there would be a substantial risk to anyone's health if I were found not to have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would there be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person if you were found not to have limited capability for work?
      `reasonable workplace adjustments could reduce that risk by a significant amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could reasonable adjustments in your workplace reduce that risk by a significant amount?
      `taking my prescribed medication could reduce that risk by a significant amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could the risk be reduced by a significant amount by you taking medication prescribed by the registered medical practitioner treating you?
      `I suffer from a life threatening disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a life threatening disease?
      `there is medical evidence that my disease is uncontrollable by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there medical evidence that your disease is uncontrollable by a recognised therapeutic procedure?
      `there is medical evidence that my disease is uncontrolled by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there medical evidence that your disease is uncontrolled by a recognised therapeutic procedure?
      `there is a reasonable cause for my disease not to be controlled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a reasonable cause for your disease not to be controlled by a recognised therapeutic procedure?
      `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the qualifying age for state pension credit?
      `the benefits I am entitled to` IS A LIST OF Benefit @desc Which of these benefits are you entitled to? Choose all that apply, or none.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having limited capability for work because of my circumstances` IF
    `reg 39(6) and (7) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work` `my circumstances` `my assessment under this Part has found limited capability for work`
    WHERE
        `my circumstances` MEANS `Sch 8 circumstances` WITH
            `paragraph 1 facts` IS `my paragraph 1 facts`
            `paragraph 2 facts` IS `my paragraph 2 facts`
            `paragraph 3 facts` IS `my paragraph 3 facts`
            `paragraph 4 facts` IS `my paragraph 4 facts`
            `paragraph 5 facts` IS `my paragraph 5 facts`
            `paragraph 6 facts` IS `my paragraph 6 facts`
        `my paragraph 1 facts` MEANS `Sch 8 para 1 treatment facts` WITH
            `receiving regular weekly treatment by way of haemodialysis for chronic renal failure` IS `I receive regular weekly haemodialysis for chronic renal failure`
            `receiving treatment by way of plasmapheresis` IS `I receive plasmapheresis`
            `receiving regular weekly treatment by way of total parenteral nutrition for gross impairment of enteric function` IS `I receive regular weekly total parenteral nutrition`
            `recovering from any of those forms of treatment` IS `I am recovering from one of those treatments`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied I should be treated as having limited capability for work after that treatment`
        `my paragraph 2 facts` MEANS `Sch 8 para 2 hospital facts` WITH
            `undergoing medical or other treatment as a patient in a hospital or similar institution` IS `I am a patient in a hospital or similar institution`
            `attending a residential programme of rehabilitation for the treatment of drug or alcohol dependency` IS `I attend a residential programme of rehabilitation for drug or alcohol dependency`
            `has been advised to stay for a period of 24 hours or longer following medical or other treatment` IS `I have been advised to stay 24 hours or more after treatment`
            `adviser` IS `my adviser`
            `recovering from such treatment` IS `I am recovering from treatment as a hospital patient`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied I should be treated as having limited capability for work after hospital treatment`
        `my adviser` MEANS Practitioner WITH
            `registered medical practitioner` IS `the person who advised me is a registered medical practitioner`
            `registered nurse` IS `the person who advised me is a registered nurse`
            `occupational therapist or physiotherapist` IS `the person who advised me is an occupational therapist or physiotherapist`
            `registered with a regulatory body established under section 60 of the Health Act 1999` IS `the person who advised me is registered with a body under section 60 of the Health Act 1999`
        `my paragraph 3 facts` MEANS `Sch 8 para 3 facts` WITH
            `nation in which the claimant is` IS `the nation I live in`
            `excluded or abstains from work pursuant to a request or notice in writing lawfully made or given under an enactment` IS `I am excluded or abstain from work under a written request or notice made under an enactment`
            `otherwise prevented from working pursuant to an enactment` IS `I am otherwise prevented from working under an enactment`
            `it is known or reasonably suspected that the claimant is infected or contaminated, or has been in contact with a case` IS `it is known or suspected that I am infected or contaminated, or have been in contact with a case`
            `incidence or spread of infection or contamination within section 45A(3) of the Public Health (Control of Disease) Act 1984 for which regulations are made under Part 2A of that Act` IS `the infection or contamination is within section 45A(3) of the Public Health (Control of Disease) Act 1984`
            `tuberculosis or an infectious disease to which regulation 9 of the Public Health (Aircraft) Regulations 1979 or regulation 10 of the Public Health (Ships) Regulations 1979 applies` IS `it is tuberculosis or an infectious disease of the Public Health (Aircraft) or (Ships) Regulations 1979`
            `infectious disease within section 1(5) of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008, or exposure to an organism causing that disease` IS `it is an infectious disease within section 1(5) of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008`
            `contamination within section 1(5) of that Act, or exposure to a contaminant` IS `it is a contamination within section 1(5) of that Scottish Act`
            `sections 56 to 58 of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008 (compensation) apply to it` IS `sections 56 to 58 of the Scottish Act on compensation apply`
        `my paragraph 4 facts` MEANS `Sch 8 para 4 risk facts` WITH
            `suffering from a specific illness, disease or disablement` IS `I suffer from a specific illness, disease or disablement`
            `by reason of it there would be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person were the claimant found not to have limited capability for work` IS `there would be a substantial risk to anyone's health if I were found not to have limited capability for work`
            `the risk could be reduced by a significant amount by reasonable adjustments being made in the claimant's workplace` IS `reasonable workplace adjustments could reduce that risk by a significant amount`
            `the risk could be reduced by a significant amount by the claimant taking medication prescribed by a registered medical practitioner treating the claimant` IS `taking my prescribed medication could reduce that risk by a significant amount`
        `my paragraph 5 facts` MEANS `Sch 8 para 5 disease facts` WITH
            `suffering from a life threatening disease` IS `I suffer from a life threatening disease`
            `there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrollable by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS `there is medical evidence that my disease is uncontrollable by a recognised therapeutic procedure`
            `there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrolled by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS `there is medical evidence that my disease is uncontrolled by a recognised therapeutic procedure`
            `there is a reasonable cause for the disease not to be controlled by a recognised therapeutic procedure` IS `there is a reasonable cause for my disease not to be controlled`
        `my paragraph 6 facts` MEANS `Sch 8 para 6 facts` WITH
            `reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit`
            `entitled to` IS `the benefits I am entitled to`

-- Regulation 40(2), (3) and (4) with Schedule 7. "Limited capability for work and work-related activity" is the status that
-- also lifts every work-related requirement (regulation 99 and section 19 of the Act) and raises the award. The person states which of
-- the 22 Schedule 7 descriptors apply to them most of the time, and which of those come from a specific bodily disease or disablement,
-- from treatment for a physical disease, from a mental illness or disablement, or from treatment for a mental illness. The two
-- judgments the text does not assign to anyone by name are asked as facts.
@export Do I have limited capability for work and work-related activity on the descriptors that apply to me (reg 40(2) to (4), Schedule 7)?
GIVEN `descriptors that apply to me most of the time` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Which of the Schedule 7 descriptors (1 to 14, 15(a) to (d), 16(a) to (d)) apply to you for the majority of the time, or on the majority of the occasions when you try the activity? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors that come from my bodily disease or disablement` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Of those, which come from a specific bodily disease or disablement? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors that come from treatment for my physical disease` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Of those, which are a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors that come from my mental illness or disablement` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Of those, which come from a specific mental illness or disablement? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors that come from treatment for my mental illness` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Of those, which are a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `my capability for work and work-related activity is limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your capability for work and work-related activity limited by your physical or mental condition?
      `it is not reasonable to require me to undertake such activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the limit such that it is not reasonable to require you to undertake work and work-related activity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have limited capability for work and work-related activity on the descriptors` IF
    `reg 40(2) — limited capability for work and work-related activity on the basis of an assessment under this Part` `my facts` `my capability for work and work-related activity is limited` `it is not reasonable to require me to undertake such activity`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Sch 7 claimant facts` WITH
            `descriptors that apply for the majority of the time or on the majority of the occasions` IS `descriptors that apply to me most of the time`
            `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific bodily disease or disablement` IS `descriptors that come from my bodily disease or disablement`
            `descriptors whose incapability is a direct result of treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement` IS `descriptors that come from treatment for my physical disease`
            `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific mental illness or disablement` IS `descriptors that come from my mental illness or disablement`
            `descriptors whose incapability is a direct result of treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement` IS `descriptors that come from treatment for my mental illness`
            -- Placeholders: regulation 40(2) does not read the next nine fields (regulation 40A reads them).
            `descriptors that apply at all times or on all the occasions` IS EMPTY
            `descriptors that will so apply for the rest of the claimant's life` IS EMPTY
            `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific bodily disease or disablement that the claimant will have for the rest of their life` IS EMPTY
            `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific bodily disease or disablement that has been diagnosed` IS EMPTY
            `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific mental illness or disablement that the claimant will have for the rest of their life` IS EMPTY
            `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific mental illness or disablement that has been diagnosed` IS EMPTY
            `professional who made the diagnosis` IS `no diagnosing professional`
            `professional who made the diagnosis is appropriately qualified` IS FALSE
            `services in the course of which the diagnosis was made` IS `no NHS services`
        `no diagnosing professional` MEANS Practitioner WITH
            `registered medical practitioner` IS FALSE
            `registered nurse` IS FALSE
            `occupational therapist or physiotherapist` IS FALSE
            `registered with a regulatory body established under section 60 of the Health Act 1999` IS FALSE
        `no NHS services` MEANS `Services in the course of which a diagnosis was made` WITH
            `health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service Act 2006` IS FALSE
            `health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006` IS FALSE
            `health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978` IS FALSE
            `health and social care within the meaning of the Health and Social Care (Reform) Act (Northern Ireland) 2009 provided for the purposes of the system promoted under section 2(1) of that Act` IS FALSE

-- Regulation 40(5) and (6) with Schedule 9. A claimant in one of the Schedule 9 circumstances is treated as having limited capability
-- for work and work-related activity whatever the assessment would find, unless the assessment under this Part has already found it.
@export Am I treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity because of my illness, pregnancy, treatment, risk or age (reg 40(5) and (6), Schedule 9)?
GIVEN `my assessment under this Part has found limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an assessment of your capability for work (the work capability assessment) found that you have limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `I suffer from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a progressive disease?
      `months within which death from my disease can reasonably be expected` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many months can death in consequence of that disease reasonably be expected? (0 if not applicable)
      `I am pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you pregnant?
      `there is a serious risk to my health or my unborn child's if I do not refrain from work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a serious risk of damage to your health or to the health of your unborn child if you do not refrain from work and work-related activity?
      `I receive chemotherapy or radiotherapy for cancer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you receiving treatment for cancer by way of chemotherapy or radiotherapy?
      `I am likely to receive such treatment within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you likely to receive such treatment within 6 months after the date of the determination of your capability for work and work-related activity?
      `I am recovering from cancer treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you recovering from such treatment?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied I should be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity after cancer treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that you should be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `I suffer from a specific illness, disease or disablement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a specific illness, disease or disablement?
      `there would be a substantial risk to anyone's health if I were found not to have limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would there be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person if you were found not to have limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the qualifying age for state pension credit?
      `the benefits I am entitled to` IS A LIST OF Benefit @desc Which of these benefits are you entitled to? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `I am entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate?
      `I am entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate (in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025)?
      `I am entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate?
      `I am entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate (in accordance with regulation 5(3) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity because of my circumstances` IF
    `reg 40(5) and (6) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity` `my circumstances` `my assessment under this Part has found limited capability for work and work-related activity`
    WHERE
        `my circumstances` MEANS `Sch 9 circumstances` WITH
            `paragraph 1 facts` IS `my paragraph 1 facts`
            `paragraph 2 facts` IS `my paragraph 2 facts`
            `paragraph 3 facts` IS `my paragraph 3 facts`
            `paragraph 4 facts` IS `my paragraph 4 facts`
            `paragraph 5 facts` IS `my paragraph 5 facts`
        `my paragraph 1 facts` MEANS Illness WITH
            `suffering from a progressive disease` IS `I suffer from a progressive disease`
            `months within which death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected` IS `months within which death from my disease can reasonably be expected`
        `my paragraph 2 facts` MEANS `Sch 9 para 2 pregnancy facts` WITH
            `a pregnant woman` IS `I am pregnant`
            `there is a serious risk of damage to her health or to the health of her unborn child if she does not refrain from work and work-related activity` IS `there is a serious risk to my health or my unborn child's if I do not refrain from work`
        `my paragraph 3 facts` MEANS `Sch 9 para 3 cancer treatment facts` WITH
            `receiving treatment for cancer by way of chemotherapy or radiotherapy` IS `I receive chemotherapy or radiotherapy for cancer`
            `likely to receive such treatment within 6 months after the date of the determination of capability for work and work-related activity` IS `I am likely to receive such treatment within 6 months`
            `recovering from such treatment` IS `I am recovering from cancer treatment`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied I should be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity after cancer treatment`
        `my paragraph 4 facts` MEANS `Sch 9 para 4 risk facts` WITH
            `suffering from a specific illness, disease or disablement` IS `I suffer from a specific illness, disease or disablement`
            `by reason of it there would be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person were the claimant found not to have limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS `there would be a substantial risk to anyone's health if I were found not to have limited capability for work and work-related activity`
        `my paragraph 5 facts` MEANS `Sch 9 para 5 facts` WITH
            `reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit`
            `entitled to` IS `the benefits I am entitled to`
            `entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate` IS `I am entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate`
            `entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `I am entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate`
            `entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate` IS `I am entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate`
            `entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate in accordance with regulation 5(3) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022` IS `I am entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate`

-- Regulation 40A(2) to (5). A "severe conditions criteria claimant" has limited capability for work and work-related activity and has
-- at least one Schedule 7 descriptor that constantly applies and will do so for the rest of their life, from a bodily or mental
-- condition diagnosed by an appropriately qualified health care professional in the course of NHS services.
@export Am I a severe conditions criteria claimant on the descriptors that apply to me (reg 40A, Schedule 7)?
GIVEN `descriptors that apply to me most of the time` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Which of the Schedule 7 descriptors (1 to 14, 15(a) to (d), 16(a) to (d)) apply to you for the majority of the time, or on the majority of the occasions when you try the activity? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors that come from my bodily disease or disablement` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Of those, which come from a specific bodily disease or disablement? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors that come from treatment for my physical disease` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Of those, which are a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors that come from my mental illness or disablement` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Of those, which come from a specific mental illness or disablement? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors that come from treatment for my mental illness` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Of those, which are a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors that apply to me all the time` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Which of the Schedule 7 descriptors apply to you at all times, or on all the occasions when you try the activity? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors that will apply for the rest of my life` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Which of the Schedule 7 descriptors will apply to you for the rest of your life? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors from a bodily disease I will have for life` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Which descriptors come from a specific bodily disease or disablement that you will have for the rest of your life? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors from a bodily disease that has been diagnosed` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Which descriptors come from a specific bodily disease or disablement that has been diagnosed? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors from a mental illness I will have for life` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Which descriptors come from a specific mental illness or disablement that you will have for the rest of your life? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `descriptors from a mental illness that has been diagnosed` IS A LIST OF `Sch 7 descriptor` @desc Which descriptors come from a specific mental illness or disablement that has been diagnosed? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `the professional who diagnosed me is a registered medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the diagnosis made by a registered medical practitioner?
      `the professional who diagnosed me is a registered nurse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the diagnosis made by a registered nurse?
      `the professional who diagnosed me is an occupational therapist or physiotherapist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the diagnosis made by an occupational therapist or physiotherapist?
      `the professional who diagnosed me is registered with a body under section 60 of the Health Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that occupational therapist or physiotherapist registered with a regulatory body established by Order in Council under section 60 of the Health Act 1999?
      `the professional who diagnosed me is appropriately qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the professional who made the diagnosis appropriately qualified?
      `I was diagnosed in the health service in England` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the diagnosis made in the course of health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service Act 2006?
      `I was diagnosed in the health service in Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the diagnosis made in the course of health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006?
      `I was diagnosed in the health service in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the diagnosis made in the course of health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978?
      `I was diagnosed in the health service in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the diagnosis made in the course of health and social care within the meaning of the Health and Social Care (Reform) Act (Northern Ireland) 2009, provided for the purposes of the system promoted under section 2(1) of that Act?
      `my capability for work and work-related activity is limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your capability for work and work-related activity limited by your physical or mental condition?
      `it is not reasonable to require me to undertake such activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the limit such that it is not reasonable to require you to undertake work and work-related activity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a severe conditions criteria claimant on the descriptors` IF
    `reg 40A(2) — severe conditions criteria claimant on the basis of an assessment under this Part` `my facts` `my capability for work and work-related activity is limited` `it is not reasonable to require me to undertake such activity`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Sch 7 claimant facts` WITH
            `descriptors that apply for the majority of the time or on the majority of the occasions` IS `descriptors that apply to me most of the time`
            `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific bodily disease or disablement` IS `descriptors that come from my bodily disease or disablement`
            `descriptors whose incapability is a direct result of treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement` IS `descriptors that come from treatment for my physical disease`
            `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific mental illness or disablement` IS `descriptors that come from my mental illness or disablement`
            `descriptors whose incapability is a direct result of treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement` IS `descriptors that come from treatment for my mental illness`
            `descriptors that apply at all times or on all the occasions` IS `descriptors that apply to me all the time`
            `descriptors that will so apply for the rest of the claimant's life` IS `descriptors that will apply for the rest of my life`
            `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific bodily disease or disablement that the claimant will have for the rest of their life` IS `descriptors from a bodily disease I will have for life`
            `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific bodily disease or disablement that has been diagnosed` IS `descriptors from a bodily disease that has been diagnosed`
            `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific mental illness or disablement that the claimant will have for the rest of their life` IS `descriptors from a mental illness I will have for life`
            `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific mental illness or disablement that has been diagnosed` IS `descriptors from a mental illness that has been diagnosed`
            `professional who made the diagnosis` IS `my diagnosing professional`
            `professional who made the diagnosis is appropriately qualified` IS `the professional who diagnosed me is appropriately qualified`
            `services in the course of which the diagnosis was made` IS `my NHS services`
        `my diagnosing professional` MEANS Practitioner WITH
            `registered medical practitioner` IS `the professional who diagnosed me is a registered medical practitioner`
            `registered nurse` IS `the professional who diagnosed me is a registered nurse`
            `occupational therapist or physiotherapist` IS `the professional who diagnosed me is an occupational therapist or physiotherapist`
            `registered with a regulatory body established under section 60 of the Health Act 1999` IS `the professional who diagnosed me is registered with a body under section 60 of the Health Act 1999`
        `my NHS services` MEANS `Services in the course of which a diagnosis was made` WITH
            `health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service Act 2006` IS `I was diagnosed in the health service in England`
            `health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006` IS `I was diagnosed in the health service in Wales`
            `health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978` IS `I was diagnosed in the health service in Scotland`
            `health and social care within the meaning of the Health and Social Care (Reform) Act (Northern Ireland) 2009 provided for the purposes of the system promoted under section 2(1) of that Act` IS `I was diagnosed in the health service in Northern Ireland`

-- Regulation 41(1) to (6). The Secretary of State may assess a claimant when it is the first time, or when there has been a decision
-- and the Secretary of State wishes to look at a change in condition or a mistake; but not (2) when the claimant earns at least the
-- threshold (16 hours a week at the regulation 4 rate), unless they get one of seven disability benefits or the assessment reviews an
-- earlier decision of a listed kind; and not (4), (5) again without relevant evidence after a "not limited" or "not severe" decision.
@export May the Secretary of State carry out an assessment of my capability for work (reg 41)?
GIVEN `this is the first time it falls to be determined whether I have limited capability for work, limited capability for work and work-related activity, or am a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the first time it is being decided whether you have limited capability for work, or for work and work-related activity, or are a severe conditions criteria claimant?
      `there has been a previous determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there already been a decision on that?
      `the Secretary of State wishes to look at a change in my condition or a mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State wish to determine whether there has been a relevant change in your physical or mental condition, or whether the earlier decision was made in ignorance of, or on a mistake as to, some material fact?
      `my monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your monthly earnings, in pounds?
      `the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hourly rate set by regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations that applies to you, in pounds?
      `the benefits I am entitled to` IS A LIST OF Benefit @desc Which of these benefits are you entitled to? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `the assessment would review a decision that I have limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assessment for reviewing an earlier decision that you have limited capability for work, or for work and work-related activity, made on an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations?
      `the assessment would review a decision that I am a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assessment for reviewing an earlier decision that you are a severe conditions criteria claimant, made on an assessment under this Part?
      `I was found not to have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found, on an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations, not to have limited capability for work?
      `I was found to be a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found, on an assessment under this Part, to be a severe conditions criteria claimant?
      `I was found to have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found, on an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations, to have limited capability for work?
      `I was found not to be a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found, on an assessment under this Part, not to be a severe conditions criteria claimant?
      `the new assessment would review the finding that I am not a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new assessment for reviewing the finding that you are not a severe conditions criteria claimant?
      `there is evidence that the earlier decision was made in ignorance of or on a mistake as to a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence to suggest that the earlier decision was made in ignorance of, or based on a mistake as to, some material fact?
      `there is evidence of a change in my circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence to suggest that there has been a change in your circumstances?
      `that change relates to my physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that change relate to your physical or mental condition?
      `that change consists of doing paid or voluntary work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that change consist of doing work for payment or in expectation of payment, or of doing voluntary work?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Secretary of State carry out an assessment of my capability for work` IF
    `reg 41 — the Secretary of State may carry out an assessment` `the occasion arises` `the earnings bar applies` `the bar after a decision of the first kind applies` `the bar after a decision of the second kind applies`
    WHERE
        `the occasion arises` MEANS
            `reg 41(1) — the occasion for an assessment` `this is the first time it falls to be determined whether I have limited capability for work, limited capability for work and work-related activity, or am a severe conditions criteria claimant` `there has been a previous determination` `the Secretary of State wishes to look at a change in my condition or a mistake`
        `the earnings bar applies` MEANS
            `reg 41(2) — the claimant's earnings bar an assessment` `my monthly earnings` `the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` `the benefits I am entitled to` `the kinds of review`
        `the kinds of review` MEANS `Review of a previous determination` WITH
            `the assessment is for the purposes of reviewing a previous determination that the claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity that was made on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations` IS `the assessment would review a decision that I have limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity`
            `the assessment is for the purposes of reviewing a previous determination that the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant made on the basis of an assessment under this Part` IS `the assessment would review a decision that I am a severe conditions criteria claimant`
        `the bar after a decision of the first kind applies` MEANS
            `reg 41(4) — no further assessment may be carried out` `my previous determinations` `there is relevant evidence`
        `the bar after a decision of the second kind applies` MEANS
            `reg 41(5) — no further assessment for reviewing a determination that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant may be carried out` `my previous determinations` `the new assessment would review the finding that I am not a severe conditions criteria claimant` `there is relevant evidence`
        `my previous determinations` MEANS `Previous determinations` WITH
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant does not have limited capability for work` IS `I was found not to have limited capability for work`
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS `I was found to be a severe conditions criteria claimant`
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant has limited capability for work` IS `I was found to have limited capability for work`
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS `I was found not to be a severe conditions criteria claimant`
        `there is relevant evidence` MEANS
            `reg 41(6) — relevant evidence` `there is evidence that the earlier decision was made in ignorance of or on a mistake as to a material fact` `the change the evidence suggests`
        `the change the evidence suggests` MEANS
            IF `there is evidence of a change in my circumstances`
            THEN JUST (`Change of circumstances` WITH
                `the change relates to the claimant's physical or mental condition` IS `that change relates to my physical or mental condition`
                `the change consists of doing work for payment or in expectation of payment, or doing voluntary work` IS `that change consists of doing paid or voluntary work`)
            ELSE NOTHING

-- Regulation 41(2), last limb. Where the earnings bar stops an assessment for work and work-related activity, the claimant is treated as
-- not having limited capability for work, unless treated as having it under regulation 39(6) or 40(5) (fork F-41-2 in NOTES.md: the
-- text names "limited capability for work" in the consequence, and is encoded as written).
@export Am I treated as not having limited capability for work because my earnings are too high (reg 41(2))?
GIVEN `the assessment is to decide whether I have limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assessment to decide whether you have limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `my monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your monthly earnings, in pounds?
      `the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hourly rate set by regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations that applies to you, in pounds?
      `the benefits I am entitled to` IS A LIST OF Benefit @desc Which of these benefits are you entitled to? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `the assessment would review a decision that I have limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assessment for reviewing an earlier decision that you have limited capability for work, or for work and work-related activity, made on an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations?
      `the assessment would review a decision that I am a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assessment for reviewing an earlier decision that you are a severe conditions criteria claimant, made on an assessment under this Part?
      `I am treated as having limited capability for work under regulation 39(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated as having limited capability for work because of one of the circumstances in Schedule 8?
      `I am treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity under regulation 40(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity because of one of the circumstances in Schedule 9?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as not having limited capability for work because my earnings are too high` IF
    `reg 41(2) — the claimant is treated as not having limited capability for work` `the assessment is to decide whether I have limited capability for work and work-related activity` `the earnings bar applies` `I am treated as having limited capability for work under regulation 39(6)` `I am treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity under regulation 40(5)`
    WHERE
        `the earnings bar applies` MEANS
            `reg 41(2) — the claimant's earnings bar an assessment` `my monthly earnings` `the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` `the benefits I am entitled to` `the kinds of review`
        `the kinds of review` MEANS `Review of a previous determination` WITH
            `the assessment is for the purposes of reviewing a previous determination that the claimant has limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity that was made on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations` IS `the assessment would review a decision that I have limited capability for work or for work and work-related activity`
            `the assessment is for the purposes of reviewing a previous determination that the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant made on the basis of an assessment under this Part` IS `the assessment would review a decision that I am a severe conditions criteria claimant`

-- Regulation 42(2). The assessment treats the claimant as fitted with, wearing or using any prosthesis normally fitted or worn, and any
-- aid or appliance that is normally worn or used or could reasonably be expected to be.
@export Am I assessed as if I were using my prosthesis, aid or appliance (reg 42(2))?
GIVEN `I normally have a prosthesis fitted or wear one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you normally fitted with, or do you normally wear, a prosthesis?
      `I normally wear or use an aid or appliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you normally wear or use an aid or appliance?
      `I could reasonably be expected to wear or use an aid or appliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could you reasonably be expected to wear or use an aid or appliance?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I assessed as if I were using my prosthesis, aid or appliance` IF
    `reg 42(2) — the claimant is assessed as if fitted with, wearing or using it` `my item`
    WHERE
        `my item` MEANS `Prosthesis, aid or appliance` WITH
            `a prosthesis with which the claimant is normally fitted or which the claimant normally wears` IS `I normally have a prosthesis fitted or wear one`
            `an aid or appliance which is normally worn or used` IS `I normally wear or use an aid or appliance`
            `an aid or appliance which could reasonably be expected to be worn or used` IS `I could reasonably be expected to wear or use an aid or appliance`

-- Regulation 43(1) and (2). The claimant must provide any information relating to the Schedule 6 or 7 descriptors that the Secretary of
-- State requests by questionnaire (unless the Secretary of State is satisfied there is enough without it), and any additional
-- information the Secretary of State requests.
@export Must I give the information the Secretary of State has asked me for (reg 43(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `it is information about the descriptors, asked for by questionnaire` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information about the Schedule 6 or 7 descriptors, asked for by the Secretary of State in a questionnaire?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied there is enough information without it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that there is enough information to make the decision without that information?
      `it is additional information the Secretary of State has requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it additional information that the Secretary of State has requested?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the information the Secretary of State has asked me for` IF
    `reg 43(1)(a) and (2) — the questionnaire information is required` `it is information about the descriptors, asked for by questionnaire` `the Secretary of State is satisfied there is enough information without it`
    OR `reg 43(1)(b) — the additional information is required` `it is additional information the Secretary of State has requested`

-- Regulation 43(3) and (4). A claimant who fails without good reason to provide the information is treated as not having the capability
-- they claim, but only after a further request sent at least 3 weeks after the first, and 1 week having passed since it was sent.
-- The answer is the decision the person is treated as failing, or NOTHING when the consequence does not apply.
@export Am I treated as not having the capability I claim because I did not give the information (reg 43(3) and (4))?
GIVEN `the decision I am asking about` IS A `Determination in question` @desc Which decision is it: whether you have limited capability for work, whether you have limited capability for work and work-related activity, or whether you are a severe conditions criteria claimant?
      `I failed to give the information requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to provide the information the Secretary of State requested?
      `I had a good reason for failing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a good reason for failing?
      `the date of the first request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Secretary of State first ask you for the information?
      `the date a further request was sent` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date was a further request sent to you? (leave blank if none was sent)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Determination in question`
DECIDE `Am I treated as not having the capability I claim because I did not give the information` IS
    `reg 43(3) — the determination that the claimant is treated as not satisfying` `the decision I am asking about` `I failed to give the information requested` `I had a good reason for failing` `my requests` `the date I am asking about`
    WHERE
        `my requests` MEANS `Requests for information` WITH
            `date of the first request` IS `the date of the first request`
            `date on which a further request was sent` IS `the date a further request was sent`

-- Regulation 44(1). The claimant may be called to attend a medical examination by or on behalf of a health care professional approved
-- by the Secretary of State, where it falls to be decided whether they have limited capability for work, or for work and work-related
-- activity, or are a severe conditions criteria claimant.
@export May I be called to a medical examination (reg 44(1))?
GIVEN `the examiner is a registered medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who will examine you a registered medical practitioner?
      `the examiner is a registered nurse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who will examine you a registered nurse?
      `the examiner is an occupational therapist or physiotherapist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who will examine you an occupational therapist or physiotherapist?
      `the examiner is registered with a body under section 60 of the Health Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that occupational therapist or physiotherapist registered with a regulatory body established by Order in Council under section 60 of the Health Act 1999?
      `the examiner is approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State approved the examiner?
      `a decision falls to be made on my capability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it fall to be decided whether you have limited capability for work, or for work and work-related activity, or are a severe conditions criteria claimant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be called to a medical examination` IF
    `reg 44(1) — the claimant may be called to attend a medical examination` `my examiner` `the examiner is approved by the Secretary of State` `a decision falls to be made on my capability`
    WHERE
        `my examiner` MEANS Practitioner WITH
            `registered medical practitioner` IS `the examiner is a registered medical practitioner`
            `registered nurse` IS `the examiner is a registered nurse`
            `occupational therapist or physiotherapist` IS `the examiner is an occupational therapist or physiotherapist`
            `registered with a regulatory body established under section 60 of the Health Act 1999` IS `the examiner is registered with a body under section 60 of the Health Act 1999`

-- Regulation 44(2) and (3). A claimant called to a medical examination (in person, by telephone or by video) who fails without good
-- reason to attend or submit to it is treated as not having the capability they claim, if the notice gave the date, time and place and
-- was given at least 7 days ahead (or less, with the claimant's agreement). The answer is the decision the person is treated as
-- failing, or NOTHING when the consequence does not apply.
@export Am I treated as not having the capability I claim because I missed a medical examination (reg 44(2) and (3))?
GIVEN `the decision I am asking about` IS A `Determination in question` @desc Which decision is it: whether you have limited capability for work, whether you have limited capability for work and work-related activity, or whether you are a severe conditions criteria claimant?
      `I was called to an examination by or for a health care professional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you called, by or on behalf of a health care professional, to attend a medical examination in person, by telephone or by video?
      `I failed to attend or submit to the examination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to attend or submit to the examination?
      `I had a good reason for failing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a good reason for failing?
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you given notice of the examination?
      `the date of the examination` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the examination?
      `the notice gave the date, time and place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the notice give the date, time and place of the examination?
      `I agreed to accept less than 7 days' notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you agree to accept less than 7 days' notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Determination in question`
DECIDE `Am I treated as not having the capability I claim because I missed a medical examination` IS
    `reg 44(2) — the determination that the claimant is treated as not satisfying` `the decision I am asking about` `I was called to an examination by or for a health care professional` `I failed to attend or submit to the examination` `I had a good reason for failing` `my notice`
    WHERE
        `my notice` MEANS `Notice of a medical examination` WITH
            `date on which the notice was given` IS `the date the notice was given`
            `date of the examination` IS `the date of the examination`
            `the notice gave the date, time and place of the examination` IS `the notice gave the date, time and place`
            `the claimant agreed to accept less than 7 days' notice` IS `I agreed to accept less than 7 days' notice`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Whether I am a carer and how many hours I am expected to work`

-- Regulation 85, "relevant carer". A parent who is not the responsible carer for the child but has caring responsibilities for the
-- child, or a person who has caring responsibilities for a person with a physical or mental impairment.
@export Am I a relevant carer (reg 85)?
GIVEN `I am a parent of a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a parent of a child?
      `I am the responsible carer for that child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the responsible carer for that child (the parent, or in a couple the one nominated, who has the main responsibility for the child's care)?
      `I have caring responsibilities for that child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have caring responsibilities for that child?
      `I have caring responsibilities for a person with a physical or mental impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have caring responsibilities for a person who has a physical or mental impairment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a relevant carer` IF
    `reg 85 — relevant carer` `my carer facts`
    WHERE
        `my carer facts` MEANS `Relevant carer facts` WITH
            `the claimant is a parent of a child` IS `I am a parent of a child`
            `the claimant is the responsible carer for that child` IS `I am the responsible carer for that child`
            `the claimant has caring responsibilities for that child` IS `I have caring responsibilities for that child`
            `the claimant has caring responsibilities for a person who has a physical or mental impairment` IS `I have caring responsibilities for a person with a physical or mental impairment`

-- Regulation 86(4). Joint claimants may change which of them is nominated as the responsible carer (or responsible foster parent)
-- once in a 12 month period starting from the date of the previous nomination, or at any time the Secretary of State considers there
-- has been a relevant change of circumstances.
@export May my partner and I change which of us is nominated as the responsible carer (reg 86(4))?
GIVEN `the date of our previous nomination` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you and your partner last make a nomination?
      `the date we want to change it` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want to change the nomination?
      `the Secretary of State considers there has been a relevant change of circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they consider there has been a change of circumstances relevant to the nomination?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my partner and I change which of us is nominated as the responsible carer` IF
    `reg 86(4) — the joint claimants may change which member is nominated` `the date of our previous nomination` `the date we want to change it` `the Secretary of State considers there has been a relevant change of circumstances`

-- Regulation 87. In the work-related requirements, "obtaining paid work" includes obtaining more paid work or better-paid work.
@export Does getting more work or better-paid work count as obtaining paid work (reg 87)?
GIVEN `I obtain paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you obtained paid work?
      `I obtain more paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you obtained more paid work than you had?
      `I obtain better-paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you obtained better-paid work than you had?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does getting more work or better-paid work count as obtaining paid work` IF
    `reg 87 — the claimant obtains paid work, including more or better-paid work` `I obtain paid work` `I obtain more paid work` `I obtain better-paid work`

-- Regulation 88. The expected number of hours a week is 35, unless a lesser number applies to a carer, a foster parent with reasonable
-- prospects of work, a responsible carer of a child below school age or under 13, or a person with an impairment. Each lesser number is
-- what the Secretary of State considers compatible or reasonable, so the person states the number in their work-related requirements
-- notice (0 where none applies); the least number of any limb that applies is the answer.
@export How many hours a week am I expected to spend looking for work and being available for it (reg 88)?
GIVEN `I am a relevant carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a relevant carer?
      `I am a responsible carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the responsible carer for a child?
      `I am a responsible foster parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a responsible foster parent?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied I have reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that you have reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work?
      `hours compatible with my caring responsibilities (limb a)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week has the Secretary of State considered compatible with your caring responsibilities (as a relevant carer, responsible carer or responsible foster parent with reasonable prospects of work)? (0 if none)
      `my child is below compulsory school age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the responsible carer of a child who has not yet reached compulsory school age?
      `hours compatible with my caring responsibilities (limb aa)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week has the Secretary of State considered compatible with your caring responsibilities for that child? (0 if none)
      `my child is of school age and under 13` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the responsible carer of a child who has reached compulsory school age but is under 13?
      `hours compatible with my child's school hours` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week has the Secretary of State considered compatible with the child's normal school hours? (0 if none)
      `I have a physical or mental impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a physical or mental impairment?
      `hours reasonable in light of my impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week has the Secretary of State considered reasonable in light of your impairment? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours a week am I expected to spend looking for work and being available for it` IS
    `reg 88 — the expected number of hours per week` `my hours facts`
    WHERE
        `my hours facts` MEANS `Expected hours facts` WITH
            `the claimant is a relevant carer` IS `I am a relevant carer`
            `the claimant is a responsible carer` IS `I am a responsible carer`
            `the claimant is a responsible foster parent` IS `I am a responsible foster parent`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant has reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied I have reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work`
            `the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is compatible with those caring responsibilities, limb (a)` IS `hours compatible with my caring responsibilities (limb a)`
            `the claimant is a responsible carer of a child who has not yet reached compulsory school age` IS `my child is below compulsory school age`
            `the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is compatible with those caring responsibilities, limb (aa)` IS `hours compatible with my caring responsibilities (limb aa)`
            `the claimant is a responsible carer for a child who has reached compulsory school age but who is under the age of 13` IS `my child is of school age and under 13`
            `the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is compatible with the child's normal school hours` IS `hours compatible with my child's school hours`
            `the claimant has a physical or mental impairment` IS `I have a physical or mental impairment`
            `the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is reasonable in light of the impairment` IS `hours reasonable in light of my impairment`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Which work-related requirements bind me`

-- Regulation 89(1) to (4). A claimant falls within section 19 of the Act, and so is subject to no work-related requirements, if any of
-- these applies: (a) they have reached state pension credit age; (b) they care for a severely disabled person for 35 hours a week and the
-- Secretary of State is satisfied it would be unreasonable to require work search or availability; (c) they are within 11 weeks of the
-- expected week of confinement or within 15 weeks after it; (d) they are an adopter within 12 months of the placement; (da) they are a
-- member of a couple with student income; (e) they need not meet the condition of not receiving education and are a listed person or have
-- student income; (f) they are the responsible foster parent of a child under 1.
@export Am I subject to no work-related requirements because of my age, caring, pregnancy, adoption, studies or fostering (reg 89)?
GIVEN `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the qualifying age for state pension credit?
      `I care for a severely disabled person for at least 35 hours a week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have caring responsibilities for one or more severely disabled people for at least 35 hours a week?
      `I meet the conditions for a carer's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the conditions for entitlement to a carer's allowance?
      `I am entitled to carer support payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to carer support payment?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied it would be unreasonable to require me to look for work or be available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require you to comply with a work search and a work availability requirement, even if limited?
      `I am pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you pregnant?
      `the first day of my expected week of confinement` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc What is the first day of your expected week of confinement? (leave blank if you are not pregnant)
      `I was pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you pregnant, with the pregnancy now ended by confinement?
      `the date of my confinement` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date was your confinement? (leave blank if none)
      `an adoption agency has decided I would be a suitable adoptive parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an adoption agency decided that you would be a suitable adoptive parent for the child?
      `I am or am intended to be the responsible carer of the child to be adopted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or are you intended to be, the responsible carer for the child?
      `the child to be adopted is placed with me as a foster child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child placed with you as a foster child?
      `the nation where the child to be adopted is placed with me as a foster child` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc If so, in which nation is the child placed with you as a foster child? (England if not applicable)
      `that foster placement is under the placement regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child placed with you under the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review Regulations (England 2010, Wales 2015) or the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009? (no if not applicable)
      `I am a foster carer or kinship carer for that child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Scotland, are you the child's foster carer or kinship carer? (no if not applicable)
      `my relation to the child to be adopted` IS A `Listed relation` @desc Are you the child's parent, parent-in-law, son, son-in-law, daughter, daughter-in-law, step-parent, step-son, step-daughter, brother or sister? Choose which, or "not a listed relation".
      `my partner's relation to the child to be adopted` IS A `Listed relation` @desc If you have a partner, are they any of those relations of the child (the child's parent, parent-in-law, son, and so on)? Choose which, or "not a listed relation".
      `the date the child was placed with me for adoption` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the child placed with you for adoption?
      `I asked that the 12 months run from a date before the placement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask that the 12 months run from a date within 14 days before the child was expected to be placed?
      `the date I asked the 12 months to run from` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc What date did you ask the 12 months to run from? (leave blank if none)
      `I am a member of a couple entitled to universal credit by virtue of regulation 3(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a couple entitled to universal credit by virtue of regulation 3(2)(b) (a couple of whom one has reached state pension credit age or is a full-time student)?
      `I have student income that is taken into account in my award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have student income in relation to the course you are undertaking which is taken into account in the calculation of your award?
      `that income is a postgraduate loan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that income a postgraduate loan?
      `the course for which the loan is paid is a full-time course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the course for which that loan is paid a full-time course?
      `I do not have to meet the condition of not receiving education by virtue of regulation 14` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you not have to meet the condition in section 4(1)(d) of the Act (not receiving education) by virtue of regulation 14?
      `I am a person referred to in paragraph (a) of regulation 14` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person referred to in paragraph (a) of regulation 14?
      `the nation where the foster child is placed with me` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc If you foster a child, in which nation is the child placed with you? (England if not applicable)
      `the foster child is placed with me under the placement regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the foster child placed with you under the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review Regulations (England 2010, Wales 2015) or the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009? (no if not applicable)
      `I am a foster carer or kinship carer for the foster child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Scotland, are you the foster carer or kinship carer of that child? (no if not applicable)
      `my partner is also a foster parent of the foster child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner also a foster parent of that child?
      `another person who is not my partner is a foster parent of the foster child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any other person, who is not your partner, a foster parent of that child?
      `I am the member of our couple nominated under regulation 86` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you and your partner both foster the child, are you the one nominated under regulation 86?
      `the foster child is under the age of 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the foster child under the age of 1?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I subject to no work-related requirements because of my age, caring, pregnancy, adoption, studies or fostering` IF
    `reg 89(1) — the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act` `limb a` `limb b` `limb c` `limb d` `limb da` `limb e` `limb f`
    WHERE
        `limb a` MEANS `reg 89(1)(a) — the claimant has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` `I have reached the qualifying age for state pension credit`
        `limb b` MEANS `reg 89(1)(b) — the claimant cares for a severely disabled person` `my caring`
        `my caring` MEANS `Caring for a severely disabled person` WITH
            `the claimant has caring responsibilities for one or more severely disabled persons for at least 35 hours a week` IS `I care for a severely disabled person for at least 35 hours a week`
            `the claimant meets the conditions for entitlement to a carer's allowance` IS `I meet the conditions for a carer's allowance`
            `the claimant has entitlement to carer support payment` IS `I am entitled to carer support payment`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement and a work availability requirement, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) or 18(3) of the Act` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied it would be unreasonable to require me to look for work or be available`
        `limb c` MEANS `reg 89(1)(c) — the claimant is pregnant or recently confined` `my pregnancy` `the date I am asking about`
        `my pregnancy` MEANS `Pregnancy or confinement` WITH
            `the claimant is pregnant` IS `I am pregnant`
            `first day of her expected week of confinement` IS `the first day of my expected week of confinement`
            `the claimant was pregnant` IS `I was pregnant`
            `date of her confinement` IS `the date of my confinement`
        `limb d` MEANS `reg 89(1)(d) — the claimant is an adopter within 12 months of the placement` `my adopter facts` `my adoption placement` `the date I am asking about`
        `my adopter facts` MEANS `Adopter facts` WITH
            `an adoption agency has decided that the person would be a suitable adoptive parent for the child` IS `an adoption agency has decided I would be a suitable adoptive parent`
            `the person is, or is intended to be, the responsible carer for the child` IS `I am or am intended to be the responsible carer of the child to be adopted`
            `the person's placement of the child as a foster parent` IS
                IF `the child to be adopted is placed with me as a foster child`
                THEN JUST (`Placement of a child with a person` WITH
                    `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation where the child to be adopted is placed with me as a foster child`
                    `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS `that foster placement is under the placement regulations`
                    `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS `I am a foster carer or kinship carer for that child`)
                ELSE NOTHING
            `the person's relation to the child` IS `Possible close relative` WITH
                `relation to the person` IS `my relation to the child to be adopted`
                `relation of the partner to the person` IS `my partner's relation to the child to be adopted`
        `my adoption placement` MEANS `Adoption placement` WITH
            `date on which the child was placed with the claimant` IS `the date the child was placed with me for adoption`
            `the claimant requested that the 12 months should run from a date within 14 days before the child was expected to be placed` IS `I asked that the 12 months run from a date before the placement`
            `the date from which the claimant requested that the 12 months should run` IS `the date I asked the 12 months to run from`
        `limb da` MEANS `reg 89(1)(da) — a member of a couple with student income` `I am a member of a couple entitled to universal credit by virtue of regulation 3(2)(b)` `I have student income that is taken into account in my award`
        `limb e` MEANS `reg 89(1)(e) — the claimant need not meet the condition of not receiving education` `I do not have to meet the condition of not receiving education by virtue of regulation 14` `I am a person referred to in paragraph (a) of regulation 14` `my student income counts`
        `my student income counts` MEANS `reg 89(4) — the claimant is treated as having student income` `I have student income that is taken into account in my award` `that income is a postgraduate loan` `the course for which the loan is paid is a full-time course`
        `limb f` MEANS `reg 89(1)(f) — the responsible foster parent of a child under 1` `my foster parenthood` `the foster child is under the age of 1`
        `my foster parenthood` MEANS `Foster parents of a child` WITH
            `the claimant's placement of the child` IS `my placement of the foster child`
            `the other member of the couple's placement of the child` IS
                IF `my partner is also a foster parent of the foster child`
                THEN JUST (`Placement of a child with a person` WITH
                    `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation where the foster child is placed with me`
                    `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS TRUE
                    `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS TRUE)
                ELSE NOTHING
            `any other person, not a member of the couple, is a foster parent in relation to the child` IS `another person who is not my partner is a foster parent of the foster child`
            `the claimant is the member nominated in accordance with regulation 86` IS `I am the member of our couple nominated under regulation 86`
        `my placement of the foster child` MEANS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH
            `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation where the foster child is placed with me`
            `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS `the foster child is placed with me under the placement regulations`
            `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS `I am a foster carer or kinship carer for the foster child`

-- Regulation 90. A claimant falls within section 19 (no work-related requirements) if their monthly earnings reach their individual
-- threshold (16 hours a week at the minimum wage rate for their age, or for those who would otherwise have to look for work, their
-- expected hours); a couple's combined earnings reach the sum of their thresholds; an apprentice reaches 30 hours or the expected hours
-- at the apprentice rate; or they are treated as having earned income under the minimum income floor. Whole pounds only: any fraction
-- of a pound in a threshold is disregarded (regulation 6(1A)).
@export Do my earnings put me in the group with no work-related requirements (reg 90)?
GIVEN `the group I would otherwise be in` IS A `Work-related group` @desc Apart from your earnings, which group would you be in: no work-related requirements, work-focused interview only, work preparation, or all work-related requirements?
      `the hourly rate for my age under the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hourly rate that applies to your age under regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds?
      `my expected hours a week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week are you expected to spend looking for work and being available for it (regulation 88)?
      `earned income for this assessment period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your earned income for this assessment period before any deduction for income tax, national insurance or pension contributions, in pounds?
      `my earned income fluctuates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your earned income fluctuate, or is it likely to?
      `my income follows an identifiable cycle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it fluctuates, is there an identifiable cycle?
      `monthly average over one cycle` IS A NUMBER @desc If there is a cycle, what is your monthly average over the duration of one cycle, in pounds? (0 if not applicable)
      `monthly average over three months` IS A NUMBER @desc If there is no cycle, what is your monthly average over three months (or other period that determines it more accurately), in pounds? (0 if not applicable)
      `how I claim` IS A `Claim basis` @desc Do you claim as a single claimant, as joint claimants, or as a single claimant who is a member of a couple?
      `my partner's group` IS A `Work-related group` @desc If you claim jointly, which group would your partner otherwise be in? (any if not applicable)
      `my partner's hourly rate` IS A NUMBER @desc If you claim jointly, what is the hourly rate that applies to your partner's age, in pounds? (0 if not applicable)
      `my partner's expected hours a week` IS A NUMBER @desc If you claim jointly, how many hours a week is your partner expected to look for work? (0 if not applicable)
      `our combined monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are a member of a couple, what are your combined monthly earnings, in pounds? (0 if not applicable)
      `the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hourly rate specified in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (the adult rate), in pounds?
      `I am employed under a contract of apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed under a contract of apprenticeship?
      `the apprentice rate under regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rate specified in regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (the apprentice rate), in pounds? (0 if not applicable)
      `I am treated as having earned income under regulation 62` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated as having earned income in accordance with regulation 62 (the minimum income floor)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my earnings put me in the group with no work-related requirements` IF
    `reg 90 — the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by the earnings thresholds` `by paragraph (1)` `by paragraph (3)` `by paragraph (4)` `by paragraph (5)`
    WHERE
        `my monthly earnings` MEANS `reg 90(6) — the person's monthly earnings` `my earnings`
        `my earnings` MEANS `Earnings for the monthly earnings of regulation 90(6)` WITH
            `earned income calculated or estimated in relation to the current assessment period before any deduction` IS `earned income for this assessment period`
            `the person's earned income fluctuates (or is likely to fluctuate)` IS `my earned income fluctuates`
            `there is an identifiable cycle` IS `my income follows an identifiable cycle`
            `monthly average over the duration of one such cycle` IS `monthly average over one cycle`
            `monthly average over three months or such other period as may enable the monthly average to be determined more accurately` IS `monthly average over three months`
        `my threshold` MEANS `reg 90(2) — the individual threshold` `the group I would otherwise be in` `the hourly rate for my age under the National Minimum Wage Regulations` `my expected hours a week`
        `my partner's threshold` MEANS `reg 90(2) — the individual threshold` `my partner's group` `my partner's hourly rate` `my partner's expected hours a week`
        `by paragraph (1)` MEANS `reg 90(1) — the claimant's monthly earnings equal or exceed the individual threshold` `my monthly earnings` `my threshold`
        -- The couple's threshold takes the claimant's and the other joint claimant's individual thresholds; it is not available if the claimant
        -- has none. For a single claimant who is a member of a couple the other threshold is not read (the rule adds 35 hours instead).
        `by paragraph (3)` MEANS `reg 90(3) — the couple's combined monthly earnings equal or exceed the threshold` `our combined monthly earnings` `the couple's threshold`
        `the couple's threshold` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my threshold`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST mine THEN
                CONSIDER `how I claim`
                WHEN `joint claimants` THEN
                    CONSIDER `my partner's threshold`
                    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                    WHEN JUST theirs THEN `reg 90(3) — the threshold for the couple's combined monthly earnings` `how I claim` mine theirs `the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`
                WHEN `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` THEN `reg 90(3) — the threshold for the couple's combined monthly earnings` `how I claim` mine 0 `the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`
                WHEN `a single claimant` THEN NOTHING
        `by paragraph (4)` MEANS `reg 90(4) — the apprentice's monthly earnings equal or exceed the threshold` `I am employed under a contract of apprenticeship` `my monthly earnings` `my expected hours a week` `the apprentice rate under regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`
        `by paragraph (5)` MEANS `reg 90(5) — the claimant is treated as having earned income under the minimum income floor` `I am treated as having earned income under regulation 62`

-- Regulation 91(2) and (3). A claimant falls within section 20 (work-focused interview requirement only) if they are the responsible
-- foster parent of a child aged 1 or over, or of a qualifying young person with care needs, or a foster parent (not the responsible one)
-- with such a child in their care; or between placements within 8 weeks and expecting to resume fostering; or a friend or family carer
-- within 12 months who is also the responsible carer.
@export Am I subject to the work-focused interview requirement only (reg 91)?
GIVEN `the nation where the child is placed with me` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc If you foster a child, in which nation is the child placed with you? (England if not applicable)
      `the child is placed with me under the placement regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child placed with you under the Care Planning, Placement and Case Review Regulations (England 2010, Wales 2015) or the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009? (no if not applicable)
      `I am a foster carer or kinship carer for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Scotland, are you the foster carer or kinship carer of that child? (no if not applicable)
      `my partner is also a foster parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner also a foster parent of that child?
      `another person who is not my partner is a foster parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any other person, who is not your partner, a foster parent of that child?
      `I am the member of our couple nominated under regulation 86` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you and your partner both foster the child, are you the one nominated under regulation 86?
      `the person I foster is a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you foster a child?
      `the person I foster is a qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you foster a qualifying young person?
      `the person I foster is aged at least 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you foster aged 1 or over?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied the person I foster has care needs that make requirements unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that the child or qualifying young person has care needs which would make it unreasonable to require you to comply with a work search or work availability requirement, even if limited?
      `the date I last fell within the fostering cases` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did you last foster a child or qualifying young person in the cases above? (leave blank if never)
      `I have no child or qualifying young person placed with me now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have no child or qualifying young person currently placed with you?
      `I expect to resume being a foster parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you expect to resume being a foster parent?
      `I am responsible for the child I care for as a friend or family carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you responsible for a child you look after as a friend or family member?
      `I am a parent of that child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a parent of that child?
      `I am a member of a couple whose other member is a parent of that child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a couple, the other member of which is a parent of that child?
      `my partner who is that child's parent and I are both responsible for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are you and that parent both responsible for the child?
      `I was previously a member of a couple whose other member was a parent of that child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you previously a member of a couple, the other member of which was a parent of that child?
      `immediately before the couple ended I was responsible for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, were you responsible for the child immediately before you ceased to be a member of that couple?
      `since then I have continued to be responsible for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc And have you continued to be responsible for the child since then?
      `the child has no parent or their parents cannot care for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the child have no parent, or have parents who are unable to care for the child?
      `the child would otherwise be looked after by a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it likely that the child would otherwise be looked after by a local authority because of concerns about the child's welfare?
      `the date I became a friend or family carer` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you become the child's friend or family carer?
      `I am also the responsible carer of that child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you also the responsible carer of that child?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I subject to the work-focused interview requirement only` IF
    `reg 91(2) — the claimant falls within section 20 of the Act` `limb a` `limb b` `limb c` `limb d` `limb e`
    WHERE
        `limb a` MEANS `reg 91(2)(a) — the responsible foster parent of a child aged at least 1` `my fostered person`
        `limb b` MEANS `reg 91(2)(b) — the responsible foster parent of a qualifying young person with care needs` `my fostered person`
        `limb c` MEANS `reg 91(2)(c) — a foster parent who is not the responsible foster parent, with care needs` `my fostered person`
        `limb d` MEANS `reg 91(2)(d) — a foster parent between placements` `the date I last fell within the fostering cases` `I have no child or qualifying young person placed with me now` `I expect to resume being a foster parent` `the date I am asking about`
        `limb e` MEANS `reg 91(2)(e) — a friend or family carer within 12 months` `my friend or family carer facts` `the date I became a friend or family carer` `I am also the responsible carer of that child` `the date I am asking about`
        `my fostered person` MEANS `Fostered person facts` WITH
            `the claimant's foster parenthood of the person` IS `my foster parenthood`
            `the person fostered is a child` IS `the person I foster is a child`
            `the person fostered is a qualifying young person` IS `the person I foster is a qualifying young person`
            `the person fostered is aged at least 1` IS `the person I foster is aged at least 1`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the child or qualifying young person has care needs which would make it unreasonable to require the claimant to comply with a work search requirement or a work availability requirement, including if such a requirement were limited in accordance with section 17(4) or 18(3) of the Act` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied the person I foster has care needs that make requirements unreasonable`
        `my foster parenthood` MEANS `Foster parents of a child` WITH
            `the claimant's placement of the child` IS `my placement of the child`
            `the other member of the couple's placement of the child` IS
                IF `my partner is also a foster parent of the child`
                THEN JUST (`Placement of a child with a person` WITH
                    `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation where the child is placed with me`
                    `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS TRUE
                    `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS TRUE)
                ELSE NOTHING
            `any other person, not a member of the couple, is a foster parent in relation to the child` IS `another person who is not my partner is a foster parent of the child`
            `the claimant is the member nominated in accordance with regulation 86` IS `I am the member of our couple nominated under regulation 86`
        `my placement of the child` MEANS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH
            `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation where the child is placed with me`
            `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS `the child is placed with me under the placement regulations`
            `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS `I am a foster carer or kinship carer for the child`
        `my friend or family carer facts` MEANS `Friend or family carer facts` WITH
            `the claimant is responsible for the child` IS `I am responsible for the child I care for as a friend or family carer`
            `the claimant's relationship to the child` IS `my relationship to the child`
            `the child has no parent or has parents who are unable to care for the child` IS `the child has no parent or their parents cannot care for them`
            `it is likely that the child would otherwise be looked after by a local authority because of concerns in relation to the child's welfare` IS `the child would otherwise be looked after by a local authority`
        `my relationship to the child` MEANS `Relationship to a child or qualifying young person` WITH
            `person is a parent of A` IS `I am a parent of that child`
            `person is a member of a couple, the other member of which is a parent of A` IS `I am a member of a couple whose other member is a parent of that child`
            `the person and that parent are both responsible for A` IS `my partner who is that child's parent and I are both responsible for the child`
            `person was previously a member of a couple, the other member of which was a parent of A` IS `I was previously a member of a couple whose other member was a parent of that child`
            `immediately before ceasing to be a member of that couple the person was responsible for A` IS `immediately before the couple ended I was responsible for the child`
            `since then the person has continued to be responsible for A` IS `since then I have continued to be responsible for the child`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What I must do to look for and be available for work`

-- Regulation 93. The purposes of a work-focused interview are any or all of six listed purposes. An interview that has none of them is
-- not a work-focused interview.
@export Is the interview I am asked to attend a work-focused interview (reg 93)?
GIVEN `the purposes of the interview` IS A LIST OF `Purpose of a work-focused interview` @desc Which of these purposes does the interview have? Choose all that apply, or none.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the interview I am asked to attend a work-focused interview` IF
    `reg 93 — the interview has a purpose of a work-focused interview` `the purposes of the interview`

-- Regulation 94. A claimant who fails to participate in an interview offered in connection with a vacancy they were required to apply
-- for is treated as not having complied with the work search requirement to apply for that vacancy.
@export Am I treated as not having applied for a vacancy because I did not take part in the interview (reg 94)?
GIVEN `I was offered an interview in connection with the vacancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you offered an interview in connection with the vacancy?
      `I failed to take part in the interview` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to participate in the interview?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as not having applied for a vacancy because I did not take part in the interview` IF
    `reg 94 — the claimant is treated as not having complied with a work search requirement to apply for a vacancy` `I was offered an interview in connection with the vacancy` `I failed to take part in the interview`

-- Regulation 95. In a week, a claimant is treated as not having taken all reasonable action to obtain paid work unless they spent the
-- expected number of hours less the relevant deductions (or the Secretary of State is satisfied they took all reasonable action despite
-- fewer hours) and that action gave them the best prospects of work. The deductions are the time agreed for paid work, voluntary work
-- (counted up to half the expected hours), a work preparation requirement, voluntary work preparation, and temporary childcare or
-- emergencies.
@export Am I treated as not having taken all reasonable action to look for work this week (reg 95)?
GIVEN `hours I spent taking action to obtain paid work` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours this week did you spend taking action to obtain paid work?
      `my expected hours a week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week are you expected to spend looking for work and being available for it (regulation 88)?
      `hours agreed for my paid work` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours has the Secretary of State agreed for you to carry out paid work this week?
      `hours agreed for my voluntary work` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours has the Secretary of State agreed for you to carry out voluntary work this week?
      `hours agreed for my work preparation requirement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours has the Secretary of State agreed for you to carry out a work preparation requirement this week?
      `hours agreed for my voluntary work preparation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours has the Secretary of State agreed for you to carry out voluntary work preparation this week?
      `hours agreed for a temporary matter` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours has the Secretary of State agreed for you to deal with temporary childcare responsibilities, a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances this week?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied I took all reasonable action despite fewer hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that you have taken all reasonable action to obtain paid work even though you spent fewer hours than expected?
      `my action gave me the best prospects of obtaining work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the action you took give you the best prospects of obtaining work?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as not having taken all reasonable action to look for work this week` IF
    `reg 95(1) — the claimant is treated as not having complied with the work search requirement to take all reasonable action` `hours I spent taking action to obtain paid work` `my expected hours a week` `my relevant deductions` `the Secretary of State is satisfied I took all reasonable action despite fewer hours` `my action gave me the best prospects of obtaining work`
    WHERE
        `my relevant deductions` MEANS
            `reg 95(2) and (3) — the relevant deductions` `hours agreed for my paid work` `hours agreed for my voluntary work` `hours agreed for my work preparation requirement` `hours agreed for my voluntary work preparation` `hours agreed for a temporary matter` `my expected hours a week`

-- Regulation 96. A claimant who is not able and willing immediately to attend an interview offered in connection with obtaining paid
-- work is treated as not having complied with a work availability requirement, unless they need a longer period for a caring
-- responsibility (up to 1 month to take up work or 48 hours for an interview), voluntary work (up to 1 week, or 48 hours), or a
-- notice period they must serve, and are able and willing to start on that notice.
@export Am I treated as not having met the requirement to be available for work (reg 96)?
GIVEN `I am able and willing to attend an interview immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able and willing immediately to attend an interview offered in connection with obtaining paid work?
      `I am a responsible carer or a relevant carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a responsible carer or a relevant carer?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied I need a longer period because of my caring` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that, because of your caring, you need a longer period of up to 1 month to take up paid work, or up to 48 hours to attend an interview, taking account of alternative care arrangements?
      `I am able and willing to start on that notice (caring)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, once given notice for that period?
      `I am carrying out voluntary work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you carrying out voluntary work?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied I need a longer period because of my voluntary work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that, because of your voluntary work, you need a longer period of up to 1 week to take up paid work, or up to 48 hours to attend an interview?
      `I am able and willing to start on that notice (voluntary work)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, once given notice for that period?
      `I am employed under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed under a contract of service?
      `I must give notice to end my contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required by section 86 of the Employment Rights Act 1996, or by your contract, to give notice to end it?
      `I am able and willing to take up paid work when my notice ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able and willing to take up paid work once the notice period has expired?
      `I am able and willing to attend an interview on 48 hours notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able and willing to attend an interview on 48 hours' notice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as not having met the requirement to be available for work` IF
    `reg 96(1) — the claimant is treated as not having complied with a work availability requirement` `I am able and willing to attend an interview immediately` `paragraph (2) applies`
    WHERE
        `paragraph (2) applies` MEANS
            `reg 96(2) — the claimant is treated as having complied despite not being able immediately to take up paid work` `paragraph (3) applies` `paragraph (4) applies` `paragraph (5) applies`
        `paragraph (3) applies` MEANS
            `reg 96(3) — this paragraph applies to a carer` `I am a responsible carer or a relevant carer` `the Secretary of State is satisfied I need a longer period because of my caring` `I am able and willing to start on that notice (caring)`
        `paragraph (4) applies` MEANS
            `reg 96(4) — this paragraph applies to a claimant doing voluntary work` `I am carrying out voluntary work` `the Secretary of State is satisfied I need a longer period because of my voluntary work` `I am able and willing to start on that notice (voluntary work)`
        `paragraph (5) applies` MEANS
            `reg 96(5) — this paragraph applies to a claimant working out a notice period` `I am employed under a contract of service` `I must give notice to end my contract` `I am able and willing to take up paid work when my notice ends` `I am able and willing to attend an interview on 48 hours notice`

-- Regulation 97(1) and (2). For a relevant carer, a responsible carer or a person with a physical or mental impairment, work search and
-- work availability requirements must be limited to the expected number of hours a week. For anyone else this paragraph sets no limit.
@export Are my work search and availability hours limited (reg 97(2))?
GIVEN `I am a relevant carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a relevant carer?
      `I am a responsible carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the responsible carer for a child?
      `I have a physical or mental impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a physical or mental impairment?
      `my expected hours a week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week are you expected to spend looking for work and being available for it (regulation 88)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Are my work search and availability hours limited` IS
    `reg 97(2) — the hours to which a work search and work availability requirement must be limited` `I am a relevant carer` `I am a responsible carer` `I have a physical or mental impairment` `my expected hours a week`

-- Regulation 97(3). Requirements must be limited to work in a location that would normally take at most 90 minutes to travel to from
-- home and at most 90 minutes to travel from back to home.
@export Is this job within the travelling time I can be required to accept (reg 97(3))?
GIVEN `minutes the journey from home would normally take` IS A NUMBER @desc How many minutes would the journey from your home to the job's location normally take?
      `minutes the journey back home would normally take` IS A NUMBER @desc How many minutes would the journey from the job's location back to your home normally take?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this job within the travelling time I can be required to accept` IF
    `reg 97(3) — the location is within the travelling limit` `minutes the journey from home would normally take` `minutes the journey back home would normally take`

-- Regulation 97(4) and (5). For up to 4 weeks from the date of claim (or, if later, the date you stopped paid work after being in the
-- no-requirements group by your earnings), the Secretary of State may limit your search to work like your previous work or pay, if
-- satisfied you still have reasonable prospects of paid work; the Secretary of State sets the number of days.
@export Can I be required to look only for work like my previous work or pay on this date (reg 97(4) and (5))?
GIVEN `I have previously carried out work of a particular nature or at a particular level of pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you previously carried out work of a particular nature, or at a particular level of pay?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied I still have reasonable prospects of paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that you will have reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work in spite of that limitation?
      `the date I made my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your claim?
      `the date I ceased paid work after being in the no-requirements group by my earnings` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If you ceased paid work after falling within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90, on what date? (leave blank if not)
      `days the Secretary of State has set for the limitation` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days has the Secretary of State decided the limitation applies?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be required to look only for work like my previous work or pay on this date` IF
    `reg 97(4) and (5) — the work must be of a similar nature or remuneration` `I have previously carried out work of a particular nature or at a particular level of pay` `the Secretary of State is satisfied I still have reasonable prospects of paid work` `the date I made my claim` `the date I ceased paid work after being in the no-requirements group by my earnings` `days the Secretary of State has set for the limitation` `the date I am asking about`

-- Regulation 97(6). A claimant whose physical or mental impairment has a substantial adverse effect on their ability to do work of a
-- particular nature, or in particular locations, cannot be required to search for or be available for such work.
@export Can I be required to look for work that my impairment makes it hard for me to do (reg 97(6))?
GIVEN `my impairment has a substantial adverse effect on work of a particular nature or in particular places` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your physical or mental impairment have a substantial adverse effect on your ability to carry out work of a particular nature, or in particular locations?
      `the work is of that nature or in those places` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the work of that nature, or in those locations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be required to look for work that my impairment makes it hard for me to do` IF
    NOT (`reg 97(6) — a work search or work availability requirement must not relate to the work` `my impairment has a substantial adverse effect on work of a particular nature or in particular places` `the work is of that nature or in those places`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `If I have been a victim of domestic violence`
-- Only for a person who has had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against them in the last 6 months and has told the Secretary
-- of State; the form should ask "Has this happened to you?" first.

-- Regulation 98(1)(a) and (b), (2) to (4). Where the claimant has recently (within 6 months) been a victim of domestic violence by a
-- partner, former partner or family member, has told the Secretary of State, is not living at the same address, has provided evidence
-- from a person acting in an official capacity in time, and regulation 98 has not applied in the last 12 months, then for 13 consecutive
-- weeks from the date they told the Secretary of State any work-related requirement already imposed has no effect and no other may be
-- imposed.
@export Are my work-related requirements lifted on this date because of domestic violence (reg 98(1), (2) to (4))?
GIVEN `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
      `the date I told the Secretary of State` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you notify the Secretary of State that domestic violence had been inflicted on or threatened against you?
      `I told the Secretary of State in the way they specify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the Secretary of State, in the manner they specify, that domestic violence had been inflicted on or threatened against you?
      `the incident was controlling behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the incident (or pattern of incidents) controlling behaviour (an act designed to make you subordinate or dependent by isolating you from support, exploiting your resources, depriving you of the means of independence, resistance or escape, or regulating your everyday behaviour)?
      `the incident was coercive behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it coercive behaviour (an act of assault, humiliation or intimidation or other abuse used to harm, punish or frighten you)?
      `the incident was violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it violence?
      `the incident was abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it abuse, including psychological, physical, sexual, emotional or financial abuse?
      `the date the violence was inflicted or threatened` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the violence inflicted or threatened?
      `it was inflicted or threatened by my partner or former partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it inflicted or threatened by your partner or former partner?
      `the person's relation to me` IS A `Relation of a family member to the claimant` @desc If it was inflicted or threatened by someone else, is that person your grandparent, grandchild, parent, step-parent, parent-in-law, son, step-son, son-in-law, daughter, step-daughter, daughter-in-law, brother, step-brother, brother-in-law, sister, step-sister or sister-in-law? Choose which, or "not one of the relations of a family member".
      `the person's partner's relation to me` IS A `Relation of a family member to the claimant` @desc Or is that person's partner one of those relations of yours? Choose which, or "not one of the relations of a family member".
      `the last day regulation 98 applied to me` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did regulation 98 last apply to you? (leave blank if never)
      `I live at the same address as that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the date you notified the Secretary of State, were you living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the violence?
      `the date I provided the evidence` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did you provide the evidence? (leave blank if not yet)
      `I provided the evidence as soon as possible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide the evidence as soon as possible?
      `the evidence is from a health care professional of the kind regulation 98 names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a member of a profession regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the National Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002?
      `the evidence is from a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a police officer?
      `the evidence is from a social worker registered in England` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a social worker registered with Social Work England?
      `the evidence is from a social worker registered in Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a social worker registered with Social Care Wales?
      `the evidence is from a social worker registered in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a social worker registered with the Scottish Social Services Council?
      `the evidence is from a social worker registered in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a social worker registered with the Northern Ireland Social Care Council?
      `the evidence is from my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from your employer?
      `the evidence is from a representative of my trade union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a representative of your trade union?
      `the evidence is from a public, voluntary or charitable body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with you in connection with domestic violence?
      `the evidence shows my circumstances are consistent with domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the evidence demonstrate that your circumstances are consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against them during the 6 months ending on the date you notified the Secretary of State?
      `the evidence shows I made contact about such an incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the evidence demonstrate that you have made contact with that person in relation to such an incident, which occurred during that period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my work-related requirements lifted on this date because of domestic violence` IF
    `reg 98(1)(a) — a work-related requirement imposed on the claimant has no effect on the date` `this regulation applies to me` `the date I told the Secretary of State` `the date I am asking about`
    AND `reg 98(1)(b) — the Secretary of State must not impose another work-related requirement on the date` `this regulation applies to me` `the date I told the Secretary of State` `the date I am asking about`
    WHERE
        `this regulation applies to me` MEANS `reg 98(1) — this regulation applies to the claimant` `my notification facts`
        `my notification facts` MEANS `Domestic violence notification facts` WITH
            `date of the notification` IS `the date I told the Secretary of State`
            `the claimant notifies the Secretary of State, in such manner as the Secretary of State specifies, that domestic violence has been inflicted on or threatened against the claimant` IS `I told the Secretary of State in the way they specify`
            `the incident is domestic violence` IS `reg 98(4) — domestic violence` `my incident`
            `date on which the violence was inflicted or threatened` IS `the date the violence was inflicted or threatened`
            `the violence was inflicted or threatened by the claimant's partner or former partner` IS `it was inflicted or threatened by my partner or former partner`
            `the violence was inflicted or threatened by a family member` IS `reg 98(4) — family member` `my relative`
            `last day on which this regulation applied to the claimant` IS `the last day regulation 98 applied to me`
            `on the date of the notification the claimant is living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the domestic violence` IS `I live at the same address as that person`
            `date on which the claimant provided the evidence` IS `the date I provided the evidence`
            `the claimant provided the evidence as soon as possible` IS `I provided the evidence as soon as possible`
            `the evidence is from a person acting in an official capacity` IS `reg 98(4) — person acting in an official capacity` `my evidence giver`
            `the evidence demonstrates that the claimant's circumstances are consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against them during the period of 6 months ending on the date of the notification` IS `the evidence shows my circumstances are consistent with domestic violence`
            `the evidence demonstrates that the claimant has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident, which occurred during that period` IS `the evidence shows I made contact about such an incident`
        `my incident` MEANS `Incident of domestic violence` WITH
            `the incident or pattern of incidents is controlling behaviour` IS `the incident was controlling behaviour`
            `the incident or pattern of incidents is coercive behaviour` IS `the incident was coercive behaviour`
            `the incident or pattern of incidents is violence` IS `the incident was violence`
            `the incident or pattern of incidents is abuse, including psychological, physical, sexual, emotional or financial abuse` IS `the incident was abuse`
        `my relative` MEANS `Possible family member of the claimant` WITH
            `relation of the person to the claimant` IS `the person's relation to me`
            `relation of the person's partner to the claimant` IS `the person's partner's relation to me`
        `my evidence giver` MEANS `Person acting in an official capacity facts` WITH
            `a member of a profession regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the National Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002` IS `the evidence is from a health care professional of the kind regulation 98 names`
            `a police officer` IS `the evidence is from a police officer`
            `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by Social Work England` IS `the evidence is from a social worker registered in England`
            `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by Social Care Wales` IS `the evidence is from a social worker registered in Wales`
            `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by the Scottish Social Services Council` IS `the evidence is from a social worker registered in Scotland`
            `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by the Northern Ireland Social Care Council` IS `the evidence is from a social worker registered in Northern Ireland`
            `the claimant's employer` IS `the evidence is from my employer`
            `a representative of the claimant's trade union` IS `the evidence is from a representative of my trade union`
            `a public, voluntary or charitable body which has had direct contact with the claimant in connection with domestic violence` IS `the evidence is from a public, voluntary or charitable body`

-- Regulation 98(1A). Where a claimant to whom regulation 98 applies falls within section 22 of the Act and is the responsible carer of
-- a child, the Secretary of State must not impose a work search or work availability requirement for a further 13 consecutive weeks
-- beginning on the day after the first 13 weeks end.
@export May the Secretary of State impose a work search or availability requirement on me on this date after domestic violence (reg 98(1A))?
GIVEN `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
      `I fall within section 22 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fall within section 22 of the Act (are you subject to all work-related requirements)?
      `I am the responsible carer of a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the responsible carer of a child?
      `the date I told the Secretary of State` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you notify the Secretary of State that domestic violence had been inflicted on or threatened against you?
      `I told the Secretary of State in the way they specify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the Secretary of State, in the manner they specify, that domestic violence had been inflicted on or threatened against you?
      `the incident was controlling behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the incident (or pattern of incidents) controlling behaviour (an act designed to make you subordinate or dependent by isolating you from support, exploiting your resources, depriving you of the means of independence, resistance or escape, or regulating your everyday behaviour)?
      `the incident was coercive behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it coercive behaviour (an act of assault, humiliation or intimidation or other abuse used to harm, punish or frighten you)?
      `the incident was violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it violence?
      `the incident was abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it abuse, including psychological, physical, sexual, emotional or financial abuse?
      `the date the violence was inflicted or threatened` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the violence inflicted or threatened?
      `it was inflicted or threatened by my partner or former partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it inflicted or threatened by your partner or former partner?
      `the person's relation to me` IS A `Relation of a family member to the claimant` @desc If it was inflicted or threatened by someone else, is that person your grandparent, grandchild, parent, step-parent, parent-in-law, son, step-son, son-in-law, daughter, step-daughter, daughter-in-law, brother, step-brother, brother-in-law, sister, step-sister or sister-in-law? Choose which, or "not one of the relations of a family member".
      `the person's partner's relation to me` IS A `Relation of a family member to the claimant` @desc Or is that person's partner one of those relations of yours? Choose which, or "not one of the relations of a family member".
      `the last day regulation 98 applied to me` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did regulation 98 last apply to you? (leave blank if never)
      `I live at the same address as that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the date you notified the Secretary of State, were you living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the violence?
      `the date I provided the evidence` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did you provide the evidence? (leave blank if not yet)
      `I provided the evidence as soon as possible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide the evidence as soon as possible?
      `the evidence is from a health care professional of the kind regulation 98 names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a member of a profession regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the National Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002?
      `the evidence is from a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a police officer?
      `the evidence is from a social worker registered in England` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a social worker registered with Social Work England?
      `the evidence is from a social worker registered in Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a social worker registered with Social Care Wales?
      `the evidence is from a social worker registered in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a social worker registered with the Scottish Social Services Council?
      `the evidence is from a social worker registered in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a social worker registered with the Northern Ireland Social Care Council?
      `the evidence is from my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from your employer?
      `the evidence is from a representative of my trade union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a representative of your trade union?
      `the evidence is from a public, voluntary or charitable body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence from a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with you in connection with domestic violence?
      `the evidence shows my circumstances are consistent with domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the evidence demonstrate that your circumstances are consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against them during the 6 months ending on the date you notified the Secretary of State?
      `the evidence shows I made contact about such an incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the evidence demonstrate that you have made contact with that person in relation to such an incident, which occurred during that period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Secretary of State impose a work search or availability requirement on me on this date after domestic violence` IF
    NOT (`reg 98(1A) — the Secretary of State must not impose a work search or work availability requirement on the date` `this regulation applies to me` `I fall within section 22 of the Act` `I am the responsible carer of a child` `the date I told the Secretary of State` `the date I am asking about`)
    WHERE
        `this regulation applies to me` MEANS `reg 98(1) — this regulation applies to the claimant` `my notification facts`
        `my notification facts` MEANS `Domestic violence notification facts` WITH
            `date of the notification` IS `the date I told the Secretary of State`
            `the claimant notifies the Secretary of State, in such manner as the Secretary of State specifies, that domestic violence has been inflicted on or threatened against the claimant` IS `I told the Secretary of State in the way they specify`
            `the incident is domestic violence` IS `reg 98(4) — domestic violence` `my incident`
            `date on which the violence was inflicted or threatened` IS `the date the violence was inflicted or threatened`
            `the violence was inflicted or threatened by the claimant's partner or former partner` IS `it was inflicted or threatened by my partner or former partner`
            `the violence was inflicted or threatened by a family member` IS `reg 98(4) — family member` `my relative`
            `last day on which this regulation applied to the claimant` IS `the last day regulation 98 applied to me`
            `on the date of the notification the claimant is living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the domestic violence` IS `I live at the same address as that person`
            `date on which the claimant provided the evidence` IS `the date I provided the evidence`
            `the claimant provided the evidence as soon as possible` IS `I provided the evidence as soon as possible`
            `the evidence is from a person acting in an official capacity` IS `reg 98(4) — person acting in an official capacity` `my evidence giver`
            `the evidence demonstrates that the claimant's circumstances are consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against them during the period of 6 months ending on the date of the notification` IS `the evidence shows my circumstances are consistent with domestic violence`
            `the evidence demonstrates that the claimant has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident, which occurred during that period` IS `the evidence shows I made contact about such an incident`
        `my incident` MEANS `Incident of domestic violence` WITH
            `the incident or pattern of incidents is controlling behaviour` IS `the incident was controlling behaviour`
            `the incident or pattern of incidents is coercive behaviour` IS `the incident was coercive behaviour`
            `the incident or pattern of incidents is violence` IS `the incident was violence`
            `the incident or pattern of incidents is abuse, including psychological, physical, sexual, emotional or financial abuse` IS `the incident was abuse`
        `my relative` MEANS `Possible family member of the claimant` WITH
            `relation of the person to the claimant` IS `the person's relation to me`
            `relation of the person's partner to the claimant` IS `the person's partner's relation to me`
        `my evidence giver` MEANS `Person acting in an official capacity facts` WITH
            `a member of a profession regulated by a body mentioned in section 25(3) of the National Health Service Reform and Health Care Professions Act 2002` IS `the evidence is from a health care professional of the kind regulation 98 names`
            `a police officer` IS `the evidence is from a police officer`
            `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by Social Work England` IS `the evidence is from a social worker registered in England`
            `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by Social Care Wales` IS `the evidence is from a social worker registered in Wales`
            `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by the Scottish Social Services Council` IS `the evidence is from a social worker registered in Scotland`
            `registered as a social worker in a register maintained by the Northern Ireland Social Care Council` IS `the evidence is from a social worker registered in Northern Ireland`
            `the claimant's employer` IS `the evidence is from my employer`
            `a representative of the claimant's trade union` IS `the evidence is from a representative of my trade union`
            `a public, voluntary or charitable body which has had direct contact with the claimant in connection with domestic violence` IS `the evidence is from a public, voluntary or charitable body`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `When I cannot be required to look for work`
-- Regulation 99 lists the situations in which the Secretary of State must not impose a work search requirement; each paragraph is one
-- question below. A person excused by any one of them is excused.

-- Regulation 99(3) and (7). No work search requirement may be imposed on a claimant who is attending a court or tribunal as a party or
-- witness, is a prisoner, is temporarily absent for treatment (regulation 11(3)), has lost a partner or child within 6 months, is in
-- the first 6 months of structured drug or alcohol treatment, is in the first 3 months of protection arrangements under section 82 of
-- the Serious Organised Crime and Police Act 2005, or is engaged in an approved public duty.
@export Can a work search requirement be imposed on me while I am in court, prison, bereaved, in treatment, protected or on public duty (reg 99(3))?
GIVEN `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
      `I am attending a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you attending a court?
      `I am attending a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you attending a tribunal?
      `the tribunal is listed in Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that tribunal listed in Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992?
      `I am attending as a party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you attending as a party to any proceedings?
      `I am attending as a witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you attending as a witness?
      `I am detained in custody pending trial or sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction?
      `I am detained in custody under a sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court?
      `I am on temporary release from prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989?
      `I am detained in hospital under the mental health Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you detained in hospital under the Mental Health Act 1983 or the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003?
      `regulation 11(3) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 11(3) apply to you (are you temporarily absent from Great Britain for treatment or convalescence)?
      `the date my partner died` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If your partner has died, on what date? (leave blank if not)
      `the date a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for died` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If a child or qualifying young person you (or your partner) were responsible for has died, on what date? (leave blank if not)
      `the date my child died` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If your child has died, on what date? (leave blank if not)
      `I am in a structured drug or alcohol treatment course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you receiving and participating in a structured recovery-orientated course of alcohol or drug dependency treatment?
      `the date I began the treatment course` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you begin the course? (any date if not applicable)
      `protection arrangements are in place for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have arrangements been made for you by a protection provider under section 82 of the Serious Organised Crime and Police Act 2005?
      `the date the protection arrangements began to apply to me` IS A DATE @desc From what date have those arrangements applied to you? (any date if not applicable)
      `I am engaged in an approved public duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you engaged in an activity of a kind approved by the Secretary of State as being in the nature of a public duty?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a work search requirement be imposed on me while I am in court, prison, bereaved, in treatment, protected or on public duty` IF
    NOT (`reg 99(3) — this paragraph applies` `limb a` `limb b` `limb c` `limb d` `limb e` `limb f` `limb g`)
    WHERE
        `limb a` MEANS `reg 99(3)(a) — the claimant is attending a court or tribunal as a party or as a witness` `my attendance`
        `my attendance` MEANS `Attendance at a court or tribunal` WITH
            `the claimant is attending a court` IS `I am attending a court`
            `the claimant is attending a tribunal` IS `I am attending a tribunal`
            `the tribunal is listed in Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992` IS `the tribunal is listed in Schedule 1 to the Tribunals and Inquiries Act 1992`
            `the claimant is attending as a party to any proceedings` IS `I am attending as a party to the proceedings`
            `the claimant is attending as a witness` IS `I am attending as a witness`
        `limb b` MEANS `reg 99(3)(b) — the claimant is a prisoner` `my detention`
        `my detention` MEANS Detention WITH
            `detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction` IS `I am detained in custody pending trial or sentence`
            `detained in custody under a sentence imposed by a court` IS `I am detained in custody under a sentence`
            `on temporary release under the Prison Act 1952 or the Prisons (Scotland) Act 1989` IS `I am on temporary release from prison`
            `detained in hospital under the mental health Acts` IS `I am detained in hospital under the mental health Acts`
        `limb c` MEANS `reg 99(3)(c) — regulation 11(3) applies to the claimant` `regulation 11(3) applies to me`
        `limb d` MEANS `reg 99(3)(d) — any of the following persons has died within the past 6 months` `my bereavements` `the date I am asking about`
        `my bereavements` MEANS `Deaths within the past 6 months` WITH
            `date of death of the other member of the couple, where the claimant was a member of a couple` IS `the date my partner died`
            `date of death of a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant or, where the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member, was responsible` IS `the date a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for died`
            `date of death of a child, where the claimant was the child's parent` IS `the date my child died`
        `limb e` MEANS `reg 99(3)(e) — the claimant is in a course of treatment and has been for no more than 6 months` `I am in a structured drug or alcohol treatment course` `the date I began the treatment course` `the date I am asking about`
        `limb f` MEANS `reg 99(3)(f) — the claimant is under protection arrangements and has been for no more than 3 months` `protection arrangements are in place for me` `the date the protection arrangements began to apply to me` `the date I am asking about`
        `limb g` MEANS `reg 99(3)(g) — the claimant is engaged in an activity approved as being in the nature of a public duty` `I am engaged in an approved public duty`

-- Regulation 99(4), (4ZA) and (4ZB). No work search requirement may be imposed on a claimant who is unfit for work for no more than 14
-- consecutive days (and no more than 2 such periods in 12 months) and who provides a declaration for the first 7 days and, if asked,
-- a statement for any further days. Where the Secretary of State has decided the claimant has the same condition as one on which they were
-- already found, or treated as, not having limited capability for work, this applies only if the Secretary of State decides to assess
-- them under regulation 41(1)(b).
@export Can a work search requirement be imposed on me while I am unfit for work (reg 99(4), (4ZA), (4ZB))?
GIVEN `days I am unfit for work after I provide the evidence` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days are you unfit for work after the date you provide the evidence?
      `periods of unfitness for work in the last 12 months, including this one` IS A NUMBER @desc How many periods of unfitness for work have you had in the last 12 months, including this one?
      `I have provided a declaration that I am unfit for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided a declaration, in the manner and form the Secretary of State approves, that you are unfit for work?
      `I am unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days?
      `the Secretary of State has asked for a statement for those further days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State asked you for a statement for those further days?
      `I have provided a statement that I am not fit for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided a statement, given in accordance with Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Medical Evidence Regulations, that you are not fit for work?
      `I was found not to have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found, on an assessment under Part 5 or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations, not to have limited capability for work?
      `the decision I was previously treated as failing` IS A MAYBE `Determination in question` @desc If you were previously treated as not having limited capability for work, or as not having limited capability for work and work-related activity (for not giving information or not attending an examination), which decision was it? (leave blank if never)
      `in the Secretary of State's opinion the condition is the same or substantially the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Secretary of State's opinion, is the condition in your evidence the same, or substantially the same, as the condition in the evidence you gave before that decision or treatment?
      `the Secretary of State has decided to assess me under regulation 41(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State decided to carry out an assessment under regulation 41(1)(b)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a work search requirement be imposed on me while I am unfit for work` IF
    NOT (`reg 99(4) — this paragraph applies` `my unfitness facts` `paragraph (4ZB) applies` `the Secretary of State has decided to assess me under regulation 41(1)(b)`)
    WHERE
        `my unfitness facts` MEANS `Unfitness for work facts` WITH
            `days for which the claimant is unfit for work after the date that the evidence referred to in sub-paragraph (b) is provided` IS `days I am unfit for work after I provide the evidence`
            `number of such periods of unfitness for work in the period of 12 months, including this one` IS `periods of unfitness for work in the last 12 months, including this one`
            `the claimant has provided a declaration, in such manner and form as the Secretary of State approves, that the claimant is unfit for work` IS `I have provided a declaration that I am unfit for work`
            `the claimant is unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days` IS `I am unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days`
            `the Secretary of State has requested a statement for those further days` IS `the Secretary of State has asked for a statement for those further days`
            `the claimant has provided a statement given in accordance with the rules set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Medical Evidence Regulations which provides that the person is not fit for work` IS `I have provided a statement that I am not fit for work`
        -- Placeholders: regulation 99(4ZB)(a)(i) reads only the first of the four findings of a `Previous determinations` record.
        `my previous determinations` MEANS `Previous determinations` WITH
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant does not have limited capability for work` IS `I was found not to have limited capability for work`
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS FALSE
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant has limited capability for work` IS FALSE
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS FALSE
        `paragraph (4ZB) applies` MEANS `reg 99(4ZB) — this paragraph applies` `my previous determinations` `the decision I was previously treated as failing` `in the Secretary of State's opinion the condition is the same or substantially the same`

-- Regulation 99(4A) and (4C). No work search requirement may be imposed for one month on a claimant who is the responsible carer of a
-- child and, in the last 24 months, a person close to the child has died, or the child has been a victim of or witness to violence or
-- abuse (not by the claimant), with significant disruption to their childcare, once they have told the Secretary of State and the
-- Secretary of State is satisfied; the month begins on the date the Secretary of State specifies.
@export Can a work search requirement be imposed on me during a month's break after a death or abuse affecting a child in my care (reg 99(4A), (4C))?
GIVEN `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
      `the date of the event` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the death, or the violence or abuse, happen?
      `I am the responsible carer of a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the responsible carer of the child?
      `a previous responsible carer of the child has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person who was previously the responsible carer of the child died?
      `a parent of the child has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a parent of the child died?
      `a brother or sister of the child has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a brother or sister of the child died?
      `another person who normally lived with the child has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any other person who, at the time of their death, normally lived in the same accommodation as the child died?
      `that person was liable to make payments on a commercial basis for the accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that person liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect of that accommodation?
      `the child was a victim of or witness to violence or abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the child been the victim of, or witness to, an incident of violence or abuse?
      `I am the perpetrator of that violence or abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the perpetrator of that violence or abuse?
      `the event significantly disrupted my childcare responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the event resulted in significant disruption to your normal childcare responsibilities?
      `I have told the Secretary of State of the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the Secretary of State of these circumstances?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied the circumstances apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that the circumstances apply?
      `the date the Secretary of State specified for the month to begin` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date has the Secretary of State specified that the month begins? (leave blank if none yet)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a work search requirement be imposed on me during a month's break after a death or abuse affecting a child in my care` IF
    NOT ((`reg 99(4A) — the circumstances for a period of one month` `my event` `the date I am asking about`) AND (`reg 99(4C) — a period of one month under paragraph (4A) is running` `I have told the Secretary of State of the circumstances` `the Secretary of State is satisfied the circumstances apply` `the date the Secretary of State specified for the month to begin` `the date I am asking about`))
    WHERE
        `my event` MEANS `Event affecting a child in the claimant's care` WITH
            `date of the event` IS `the date of the event`
            `the claimant is the responsible carer of a child` IS `I am the responsible carer of a child`
            `a person who was previously the responsible carer of that child has died` IS `a previous responsible carer of the child has died`
            `a parent of that child has died` IS `a parent of the child has died`
            `a brother or sister of that child has died` IS `a brother or sister of the child has died`
            `any other person who, at the time of their death, normally lived in the same accommodation as that child has died` IS `another person who normally lived with the child has died`
            `that other person was liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect of that accommodation` IS `that person was liable to make payments on a commercial basis for the accommodation`
            `the child has been the victim of, or witness to, an incident of violence or abuse` IS `the child was a victim of or witness to violence or abuse`
            `the claimant is the perpetrator of that violence or abuse` IS `I am the perpetrator of that violence or abuse`
            `the event has resulted in significant disruption to the claimant's normal childcare responsibilities` IS `the event significantly disrupted my childcare responsibilities`

-- Regulation 99(4B). Only one such month may be taken in each of the four consecutive periods of 6 months after the event, and none
-- from 24 months or more after it.
@export May I take another month's break starting on this day after the same event (reg 99(4B))?
GIVEN `the date of the event` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the death, or the violence or abuse, happen?
      `the day another month's break would begin` IS A DATE @desc On what day would a further month's break begin?
      `the days earlier months' breaks began` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On what days did your earlier months' breaks for the same event begin? (none if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I take another month's break starting on this day after the same event` IF
    `reg 99(4B) — a period of one month beginning on this day is allowed` `the date of the event` `the day another month's break would begin` `the days earlier months' breaks began`

-- Regulation 99(5), (2A). No work search requirement may be imposed where the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable
-- to require it (even if limited) because the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement or voluntary work preparation, has
-- temporary child care responsibilities or a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances, is unfit for work for
-- longer or more periods than paragraph (4) allows, or would fall within paragraph (4) but for paragraph (4ZA).
@export Can a work search requirement be imposed on me when it would be unreasonable because of work preparation, a temporary matter or unfitness (reg 99(5))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State is satisfied that a work search requirement would be unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require you to comply with a work search requirement, even if limited under section 17(4) of the Act?
      `I am carrying out a work preparation requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you carrying out a work preparation requirement?
      `I am taking particular action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you taking particular action (other than a work preparation requirement) to make work more likely?
      `the Secretary of State has agreed that action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State agreed that action?
      `that action is to make it more likely I will obtain paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that action for the purpose of making it more likely that you will obtain paid work?
      `that action is specified as a work preparation requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State specified that action as a work preparation requirement under section 16 of the Act?
      `I have temporary child care responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have temporary child care responsibilities?
      `I am dealing with a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dealing with a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances?
      `days I am unfit for work after I provide the evidence` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days are you unfit for work after the date you provide the evidence?
      `periods of unfitness for work in the last 12 months, including this one` IS A NUMBER @desc How many periods of unfitness for work have you had in the last 12 months, including this one?
      `I have provided a declaration that I am unfit for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided a declaration, in the manner and form the Secretary of State approves, that you are unfit for work?
      `I am unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days?
      `the Secretary of State has asked for a statement for those further days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State asked you for a statement for those further days?
      `I have provided a statement that I am not fit for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided a statement, given in accordance with Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Medical Evidence Regulations, that you are not fit for work?
      `I was found not to have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found, on an assessment under Part 5 or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations, not to have limited capability for work?
      `the decision I was previously treated as failing` IS A MAYBE `Determination in question` @desc If you were previously treated as not having limited capability for work, or as not having limited capability for work and work-related activity (for not giving information or not attending an examination), which decision was it? (leave blank if never)
      `in the Secretary of State's opinion the condition is the same or substantially the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Secretary of State's opinion, is the condition in your evidence the same, or substantially the same, as the condition in the evidence you gave before that decision or treatment?
      `the Secretary of State has decided to assess me under regulation 41(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State decided to carry out an assessment under regulation 41(1)(b)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a work search requirement be imposed on me when it would be unreasonable because of work preparation, a temporary matter or unfitness` IF
    NOT (`reg 99(5) — this paragraph applies` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that a work search requirement would be unreasonable` `I fall within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)`)
    WHERE
        `I fall within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` MEANS
            `reg 99(5) — the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` `sub-paragraph (a)` `sub-paragraph (b)` `sub-paragraph (c)` `sub-paragraph (d)`
        `sub-paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `reg 99(5)(a) — the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement or voluntary work preparation` `I am carrying out a work preparation requirement` `I am taking particular action` `the Secretary of State has agreed that action` `that action is to make it more likely I will obtain paid work` `that action is specified as a work preparation requirement`
        `sub-paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `reg 99(5)(b) — the claimant has temporary child care responsibilities or is dealing with a temporary matter` `I have temporary child care responsibilities` `I am dealing with a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances`
        `sub-paragraph (c)` MEANS
            `reg 99(5)(c) — the claimant is unfit for work for longer or for more periods than paragraph (4)(a) allows` `my unfitness facts`
        `sub-paragraph (d)` MEANS
            `reg 99(5)(d) — paragraph (4) would apply but for paragraph (4ZA)` `my unfitness facts` `paragraph (4ZB) applies` `the Secretary of State has decided to assess me under regulation 41(1)(b)`
        `my unfitness facts` MEANS `Unfitness for work facts` WITH
            `days for which the claimant is unfit for work after the date that the evidence referred to in sub-paragraph (b) is provided` IS `days I am unfit for work after I provide the evidence`
            `number of such periods of unfitness for work in the period of 12 months, including this one` IS `periods of unfitness for work in the last 12 months, including this one`
            `the claimant has provided a declaration, in such manner and form as the Secretary of State approves, that the claimant is unfit for work` IS `I have provided a declaration that I am unfit for work`
            `the claimant is unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days` IS `I am unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days`
            `the Secretary of State has requested a statement for those further days` IS `the Secretary of State has asked for a statement for those further days`
            `the claimant has provided a statement given in accordance with the rules set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Medical Evidence Regulations which provides that the person is not fit for work` IS `I have provided a statement that I am not fit for work`
        -- Placeholders: regulation 99(4ZB)(a)(i) reads only the first of the four findings of a `Previous determinations` record.
        `my previous determinations` MEANS `Previous determinations` WITH
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant does not have limited capability for work` IS `I was found not to have limited capability for work`
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS FALSE
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant has limited capability for work` IS FALSE
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS FALSE
        `paragraph (4ZB) applies` MEANS `reg 99(4ZB) — this paragraph applies` `my previous determinations` `the decision I was previously treated as failing` `in the Secretary of State's opinion the condition is the same or substantially the same`

-- Regulation 99(5A) and (5B). The same situations can excuse the claimant from a work availability requirement: wholly (5A), where the
-- Secretary of State is satisfied it would be unreasonable to require the claimant to be available to take up paid work and to attend
-- an interview; or only from being available to take up paid work (5B), where the Secretary of State is also satisfied that it is
-- reasonable to require them to be available to attend an interview.
DECLARE `What regulation 99 excuses me from on work availability` IS ONE OF
    `no work availability requirement may be imposed on me`
    `I need not be available to take up paid work but must be available to attend an interview`
    `neither paragraph (5A) nor paragraph (5B) applies to me`

@export What work availability requirement can be imposed on me when I am preparing for work, dealing with a temporary matter or unfit (reg 99(5A) and (5B))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State is satisfied that a work availability requirement to take up work and attend an interview would be unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require you to be able and willing both to take up paid work and to attend an interview, even if limited under section 18(3) of the Act?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that a work availability requirement to take up paid work would be unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that it would be unreasonable to require you to be able and willing to take up paid work?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that a work availability requirement to attend an interview would be reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that it would be reasonable to require you to be able and willing to attend an interview, even if limited under section 18(3) of the Act?
      `I am carrying out a work preparation requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you carrying out a work preparation requirement?
      `I am taking particular action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you taking particular action (other than a work preparation requirement) to make work more likely?
      `the Secretary of State has agreed that action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State agreed that action?
      `that action is to make it more likely I will obtain paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that action for the purpose of making it more likely that you will obtain paid work?
      `that action is specified as a work preparation requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State specified that action as a work preparation requirement under section 16 of the Act?
      `I have temporary child care responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have temporary child care responsibilities?
      `I am dealing with a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dealing with a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances?
      `days I am unfit for work after I provide the evidence` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days are you unfit for work after the date you provide the evidence?
      `periods of unfitness for work in the last 12 months, including this one` IS A NUMBER @desc How many periods of unfitness for work have you had in the last 12 months, including this one?
      `I have provided a declaration that I am unfit for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided a declaration, in the manner and form the Secretary of State approves, that you are unfit for work?
      `I am unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days?
      `the Secretary of State has asked for a statement for those further days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State asked you for a statement for those further days?
      `I have provided a statement that I am not fit for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided a statement, given in accordance with Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Medical Evidence Regulations, that you are not fit for work?
      `I was found not to have limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found, on an assessment under Part 5 or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations, not to have limited capability for work?
      `the decision I was previously treated as failing` IS A MAYBE `Determination in question` @desc If you were previously treated as not having limited capability for work, or as not having limited capability for work and work-related activity (for not giving information or not attending an examination), which decision was it? (leave blank if never)
      `in the Secretary of State's opinion the condition is the same or substantially the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Secretary of State's opinion, is the condition in your evidence the same, or substantially the same, as the condition in the evidence you gave before that decision or treatment?
      `the Secretary of State has decided to assess me under regulation 41(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State decided to carry out an assessment under regulation 41(1)(b)?
GIVETH A `What regulation 99 excuses me from on work availability`
DECIDE `What work availability requirement can be imposed on me when I am preparing for work, dealing with a temporary matter or unfit` IS
    IF `reg 99(5A) — this paragraph applies` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that a work availability requirement to take up work and attend an interview would be unreasonable` `I fall within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)`
    THEN `no work availability requirement may be imposed on me`
    ELSE IF `reg 99(5B) — this paragraph applies` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that a work availability requirement to take up paid work would be unreasonable` `I fall within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that a work availability requirement to attend an interview would be reasonable`
         THEN `I need not be available to take up paid work but must be available to attend an interview`
         ELSE `neither paragraph (5A) nor paragraph (5B) applies to me`
    WHERE
        `I fall within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` MEANS
            `reg 99(5) — the claimant falls within sub-paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` `sub-paragraph (a)` `sub-paragraph (b)` `sub-paragraph (c)` `sub-paragraph (d)`
        `sub-paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `reg 99(5)(a) — the claimant is carrying out a work preparation requirement or voluntary work preparation` `I am carrying out a work preparation requirement` `I am taking particular action` `the Secretary of State has agreed that action` `that action is to make it more likely I will obtain paid work` `that action is specified as a work preparation requirement`
        `sub-paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `reg 99(5)(b) — the claimant has temporary child care responsibilities or is dealing with a temporary matter` `I have temporary child care responsibilities` `I am dealing with a domestic emergency, funeral arrangements or other temporary circumstances`
        `sub-paragraph (c)` MEANS
            `reg 99(5)(c) — the claimant is unfit for work for longer or for more periods than paragraph (4)(a) allows` `my unfitness facts`
        `sub-paragraph (d)` MEANS
            `reg 99(5)(d) — paragraph (4) would apply but for paragraph (4ZA)` `my unfitness facts` `paragraph (4ZB) applies` `the Secretary of State has decided to assess me under regulation 41(1)(b)`
        `my unfitness facts` MEANS `Unfitness for work facts` WITH
            `days for which the claimant is unfit for work after the date that the evidence referred to in sub-paragraph (b) is provided` IS `days I am unfit for work after I provide the evidence`
            `number of such periods of unfitness for work in the period of 12 months, including this one` IS `periods of unfitness for work in the last 12 months, including this one`
            `the claimant has provided a declaration, in such manner and form as the Secretary of State approves, that the claimant is unfit for work` IS `I have provided a declaration that I am unfit for work`
            `the claimant is unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days` IS `I am unfit for work for further days after the first 7 days`
            `the Secretary of State has requested a statement for those further days` IS `the Secretary of State has asked for a statement for those further days`
            `the claimant has provided a statement given in accordance with the rules set out in Part 1 of Schedule 1 to the Medical Evidence Regulations which provides that the person is not fit for work` IS `I have provided a statement that I am not fit for work`
        -- Placeholders: regulation 99(4ZB)(a)(i) reads only the first of the four findings of a `Previous determinations` record.
        `my previous determinations` MEANS `Previous determinations` WITH
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant does not have limited capability for work` IS `I was found not to have limited capability for work`
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS FALSE
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 or 5 of the ESA Regulations that the claimant has limited capability for work` IS FALSE
            `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part that the claimant is not a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS FALSE
        `paragraph (4ZB) applies` MEANS `reg 99(4ZB) — this paragraph applies` `my previous determinations` `the decision I was previously treated as failing` `in the Secretary of State's opinion the condition is the same or substantially the same`

-- Regulation 99(6) and (6A). No work search requirement may be imposed on a claimant whose monthly earnings (excluding earnings that are
-- not employed earnings) equal or exceed the amount for 18 hours a week at the regulation 4 minimum wage rate, or who is a member of a
-- couple whose combined monthly earnings reach the amount for 29 hours. Whole pounds only.
@export Can a work search requirement be imposed on me when my earnings are high enough (reg 99(6))?
GIVEN `my monthly employed earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your monthly earnings from employment, in pounds (leave out anything that is not employed earnings)?
      `how I claim` IS A `Claim basis` @desc Do you claim as a single claimant, as joint claimants, or as a single claimant who is a member of a couple?
      `our combined monthly employed earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are a member of a couple, what are your combined monthly earnings from employment, in pounds? (0 if not applicable)
      `the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hourly rate specified in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (the adult rate), in pounds?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a work search requirement be imposed on me when my earnings are high enough` IF
    NOT (`reg 99(6) — this paragraph applies` `limb (a)` `limb (b)`)
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS `reg 99(6)(a) — the claimant's monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 18 hours` `my monthly employed earnings` `the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`
        `limb (b)` MEANS `reg 99(6)(b) — the couple's combined monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 29 hours` `how I claim` `our combined monthly employed earnings` `the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`

-- Regulation 99(2) and (2A)(b). A work search requirement that applied to the claimant stops having effect from the date the
-- circumstances in paragraph (3), (4), (4A) or (6) (or (5)) begin to apply.
@export Has my work search requirement stopped having effect on this date because of one of the situations in regulation 99 (reg 99(2) and (2A)(b))?
GIVEN `the date a situation in paragraph (3), (4), (4A) or (6) began to apply to me` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did a situation in paragraph (3), (4), (4A) or (6) of regulation 99 begin to apply to you? (leave blank if none has)
      `the date the situation in paragraph (5) began to apply to me` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did the situation in paragraph (5) of regulation 99 begin to apply to you? (leave blank if none has)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my work search requirement stopped having effect on this date because of one of the situations in regulation 99` IF
    `reg 99(2) — a work search requirement previously applying has ceased to have effect` `the date a situation in paragraph (3), (4), (4A) or (6) began to apply to me` `the date I am asking about`
    OR `reg 99(2A)(b) — a work search requirement previously applying has ceased to have effect` `the date the situation in paragraph (5) began to apply to me` `the date I am asking about`

-- Regulation 99(1)(b). While a work search requirement is lifted by paragraph (3), (4), (4A) or (6), "able and willing immediately to take
-- up work" means able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, immediately once those circumstances no longer apply.
-- The answer is NOTHING when none of those paragraphs applies.
@export Am I able and willing to take up work in the way regulation 99(1)(b) requires while I am excused from work search (reg 99(1)(b))?
GIVEN `one of paragraphs (3), (4), (4A) and (6) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of paragraphs (3), (4), (4A) and (6) of regulation 99 apply to you?
      `I am able and willing to take up paid work or attend an interview once those circumstances end` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, immediately once those circumstances no longer apply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I able and willing to take up work in the way regulation 99(1)(b) requires while I am excused from work search` IS
    `reg 99(1)(b) — the claimant is able and willing immediately to take up work` `one of paragraphs (3), (4), (4A) and (6) applies to me` `I am able and willing to take up paid work or attend an interview once those circumstances end`

-- Regulation 99(2B). Where paragraph (5A) applies, "able and willing to take up work" means able and willing to take up paid work, or to attend
-- an interview, immediately once the circumstances in paragraph (5A) no longer apply. The answer is NOTHING when (5A) does not apply.
@export Am I able and willing to take up work in the way regulation 99(2B) requires while I am excused from work availability (reg 99(2B))?
GIVEN `paragraph (5A) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph (5A) of regulation 99 apply to you?
      `I am able and willing to take up paid work or attend an interview once the paragraph (5A) circumstances end` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able and willing to take up paid work, or attend an interview, immediately once the circumstances in paragraph (5A) no longer apply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I able and willing to take up work in the way regulation 99(2B) requires while I am excused from work availability` IS
    `reg 99(2B) — the claimant is able and willing to take up work` `paragraph (5A) applies to me` `I am able and willing to take up paid work or attend an interview once the paragraph (5A) circumstances end`

-- Regulation 99(2C). Where paragraph (5B) applies, "able and willing to take up work" means able and willing to take up paid work immediately
-- once the circumstances in paragraph (5B) no longer apply, and able and willing to attend an interview before then. The answer is NOTHING
-- when (5B) does not apply.
@export Am I able and willing to take up work in the way regulation 99(2C) requires while I am excused from taking up paid work (reg 99(2C))?
GIVEN `paragraph (5B) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph (5B) of regulation 99 apply to you?
      `I am able and willing to take up paid work once the paragraph (5B) circumstances end` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able and willing to take up paid work immediately once the circumstances in paragraph (5B) no longer apply?
      `I am able and willing to attend an interview before the paragraph (5B) circumstances end` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able and willing to attend an interview before those circumstances no longer apply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I able and willing to take up work in the way regulation 99(2C) requires while I am excused from taking up paid work` IS
    `reg 99(2C) — the claimant is able and willing to take up work` `paragraph (5B) applies to me` `I am able and willing to take up paid work once the paragraph (5B) circumstances end` `I am able and willing to attend an interview before the paragraph (5B) circumstances end`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What happens to my award if I fail a requirement`
-- Only for a person who may have failed a work-related requirement or done something that can lead to a reduction (a sanction); the form
-- should ask "Has this happened to you?" first.

-- Regulation 100(1) and (1A). A failure sanctionable under section 26 or 27 of the Act is a "sanctionable failure", and a "current"
-- one is one the Secretary of State has not yet determined whether to reduce the award for.
@export Is this a sanctionable failure that the Secretary of State has yet to decide on (reg 100(1) and (1A))?
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 26 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the failure one that is sanctionable under section 26 of the Act (a high-level failure)?
      `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the failure one that is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act (a failure to comply with a work-related requirement)?
      `the Secretary of State has decided whether to reduce my award for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State already determined whether the amount of your award of universal credit is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act in relation to the failure?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a sanctionable failure that the Secretary of State has yet to decide on` IF
    `reg 100(1A) — a current sanctionable failure` (`reg 100(1) — a sanctionable failure` `the failure is sanctionable under section 26 of the Act` `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act`) `the Secretary of State has decided whether to reduce my award for it`

-- Regulation 101(2). Reduction periods run consecutively: a further period can run from the day after the one before it ends.
@export On what day can my next reduction period begin to run (reg 101(2))?
GIVEN `the last day of my earlier reduction period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your earlier reduction period?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day can my next reduction period begin to run` IS
    `reg 101(2) — the first day on which the next reduction period can run` `the last day of my earlier reduction period`

-- Regulation 101(3) and (5). The total outstanding reduction period (the days of reduction not yet applied) cannot exceed 1095 days; a new
-- period is cut to what remains of the 1095.
@export How many days will my new reduction period last once the 1095-day limit is applied (reg 101(3) and (5))?
GIVEN `the reduction period calculated for this failure` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days is the reduction period calculated for this failure (under regulations 102 to 105)?
      `the days of my earlier reduction periods not yet applied` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each earlier reduction period, how many days have not yet been applied? (none if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days will my new reduction period last once the 1095-day limit is applied` IS
    `reg 101(3) — the reduction period adjusted so that the total outstanding reduction period does not exceed 1095 days` `the reduction period calculated for this failure` (`reg 101(5) — the total outstanding reduction period` `the days of my earlier reduction periods not yet applied`)

-- Regulation 102. Higher-level sanction: for a failure under section 26 of the Act the reduction is 91 days (14 days for a claimant aged
-- 16 or 17), and more where an earlier higher-level failure was recent: the table takes the claimant's age on the date of the failure, how
-- recent the most recent earlier higher-level failure was (not within 365 days, within 365 but not within 14, or within 14) and how long its
-- reduction was. A pre-claim failure gets the lesser of that period and the days left of any limited period of paid work, less the days
-- before the claim.
@export How many days is my reduction period for a higher-level failure (reg 102)?
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 26 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the failure one that is sanctionable under section 26 of the Act?
      `the failure was before I claimed (a pre-claim failure under section 26(4))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a failure sanctionable under section 26(4) of the Act (a pre-claim failure)?
      `my age on the date of the failure` IS A NUMBER @desc How old were you on the date of the failure?
      `the date of the failure` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the failure?
      `I have an earlier failure that gave rise to a higher-level sanction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you had an earlier sanctionable failure that gave rise to a higher-level sanction?
      `the date of that earlier failure` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the most recent such failure? (any date if none)
      `the reduction period that applied to that earlier failure in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days was the reduction period for that earlier failure? (0 if none)
      `that earlier failure was a pre-claim failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that earlier failure a pre-claim failure?
      `the date of my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you claim universal credit?
      `the date the limited period of my paid work would have ended` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc If the failure was to do with paid work that was due to last a limited period, on what date would that period have ended? (leave blank if not)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days is my reduction period for a higher-level failure` IS
    IF NOT (`reg 102(1) — this regulation specifies the reduction period for the failure` `the failure is sanctionable under section 26 of the Act`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `reg 102(5) — a pre-claim failure` `the failure was before I claimed (a pre-claim failure under section 26(4))`
         THEN `reg 102(4) — the reduction period for a pre-claim failure` `the period under paragraph (2)` `the date of the failure` `the date the limited period of my paid work would have ended` `the date of my claim`
         ELSE `the period under paragraph (2)`
    WHERE
        `the period under paragraph (2)` MEANS
            `reg 102(2) — the reduction period for a sanctionable failure that is not a pre-claim failure` `my age on the date of the failure` `the date of the failure` `my earlier failures`
        `my earlier failures` MEANS
            IF `I have an earlier failure that gave rise to a higher-level sanction`
            THEN LIST (`Previous sanctionable failure` WITH
                `date of the previous sanctionable failure` IS `the date of that earlier failure`
                `reduction period applicable to the previous sanctionable failure, in days` IS `the reduction period that applied to that earlier failure in days`
                `the previous sanctionable failure was a pre-claim failure` IS `that earlier failure was a pre-claim failure`
                `the previous sanctionable failure gave rise to a higher-level sanction` IS TRUE
                -- Placeholders: regulation 102 does not read the next two fields.
                `the previous sanctionable failure falls within regulation 103(1)` IS FALSE
                `the previous sanctionable failure falls within regulation 104(1)` IS FALSE)
            ELSE EMPTY

-- Regulation 103. Medium-level sanction: for a failure under section 27 to comply with a work search requirement to take all reasonable
-- action to obtain paid work (section 17(1)(a)) or a work availability requirement (section 18(1)), the reduction is 28 days (7 days for a
-- claimant aged 16 or 17), and more where an earlier failure of that kind was recent: the table takes the claimant's age, how recent the
-- most recent earlier failure of that kind was and how long its reduction was.
@export How many days is my reduction period for a medium-level failure (reg 103)?
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the failure one that is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act?
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a work search requirement under section 17(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a failure to comply with a work search requirement under section 17(1)(a) of the Act (to take all reasonable action to obtain paid work)?
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a work availability requirement under section 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a failure to comply with a work availability requirement under section 18(1) of the Act?
      `my age on the date of the failure` IS A NUMBER @desc How old were you on the date of the failure?
      `the date of the failure` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the failure?
      `I have an earlier failure of the same kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you had an earlier sanctionable failure of this kind (a failure under section 17(1)(a) or 18(1))?
      `the date of that earlier failure` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the most recent such failure? (any date if none)
      `the reduction period that applied to that earlier failure in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days was the reduction period for that earlier failure? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days is my reduction period for a medium-level failure` IS
    IF `reg 103(1) — this regulation specifies the reduction period for the failure` `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` `the failure is a failure to comply with a work search requirement under section 17(1)(a)` `the failure is a failure to comply with a work availability requirement under section 18(1)`
    THEN `reg 103(2) — the reduction period for a failure within paragraph (1)` `my age on the date of the failure` `the date of the failure` `my earlier failures`
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `my earlier failures` MEANS
            IF `I have an earlier failure of the same kind`
            THEN LIST (`Previous sanctionable failure` WITH
                `date of the previous sanctionable failure` IS `the date of that earlier failure`
                `reduction period applicable to the previous sanctionable failure, in days` IS `the reduction period that applied to that earlier failure in days`
                -- Placeholders: regulation 103 reads only the date, the reduction period and whether the failure falls within regulation 103(1).
                `the previous sanctionable failure was a pre-claim failure` IS FALSE
                `the previous sanctionable failure gave rise to a higher-level sanction` IS FALSE
                `the previous sanctionable failure falls within regulation 103(1)` IS TRUE
                `the previous sanctionable failure falls within regulation 104(1)` IS FALSE)
            ELSE EMPTY

-- Regulation 104. Low-level sanction: for a failure under section 27 by a claimant within section 21 or 22 of the Act to comply with a
-- work-focused interview, work preparation or certain other requirements, the reduction lasts until the soonest of the day before the
-- claimant meets a compliance condition, the day before they fall within section 19, the day before they are no longer required to take
-- a work preparation action, or the day the award ends, plus (for a claimant aged 18 or over) 7, 14 or 28 days according to how recent
-- and how long the most recent earlier failure of that kind was; for a claimant aged 16 or 17, plus 7 days if there was another such
-- failure within 365 days but not within 14.
@export How many days is my reduction period for a low-level failure (reg 104)?
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the failure one that is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act?
      `the work-related group I am in` IS A `Work-related group` @desc Which group are you in: no work-related requirements, work-focused interview only, work preparation, or all work-related requirements?
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a work-focused interview requirement under section 15(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a failure to comply with a work-focused interview requirement under section 15(1) of the Act?
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a work preparation requirement under section 16(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a failure to comply with a work preparation requirement under section 16(1) of the Act?
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a work search requirement under section 17(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a failure to comply with a work search requirement under section 17(1)(b) of the Act (to apply for a particular vacancy)?
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a requirement under section 23(1), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a failure to comply with a requirement under section 23(1), (3) or (4) of the Act?
      `my age on the date of the failure` IS A NUMBER @desc How old were you on the date of the failure?
      `the date of the failure` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the failure?
      `the date I met a compliance condition` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did you meet a compliance condition set by the Secretary of State? (leave blank if you have not)
      `the date I fell within section 19` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did you fall within section 19 of the Act? (leave blank if you have not)
      `the date I stopped being required to take a work preparation action` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date were you no longer required to take the particular action specified as a work preparation requirement? (leave blank if you still are)
      `the date my award ended` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did your award end, other than by your ceasing to be or becoming a member of a couple? (leave blank if it has not)
      `I have an earlier failure of the same kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you had an earlier sanctionable failure of this kind (within regulation 104(1))?
      `the date of that earlier failure` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the most recent such failure? (any date if none)
      `the reduction period that applied to that earlier failure in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days was the reduction period for that earlier failure? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days is my reduction period for a low-level failure` IS
    IF NOT (`reg 104(1) — this regulation specifies the reduction period for the failure` `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` `the work-related group I am in` `the failure is a failure to comply with a work-focused interview requirement under section 15(1)` `the failure is a failure to comply with a work preparation requirement under section 16(1)` `the failure is a failure to comply with a work search requirement under section 17(1)(b)` `the failure is a failure to comply with a requirement under section 23(1), (3) or (4)`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `reg 102(2) — the age band of the claimant on the date of the sanctionable failure` `my age on the date of the failure`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST band THEN
             CONSIDER band
             WHEN `aged 18 or over` THEN `reg 104(2) — the reduction period of a claimant aged 18 or over` `my age on the date of the failure` `the date of the failure` `the days to the soonest event` `my earlier failures`
             WHEN `aged 16 or 17` THEN `reg 104(3) — the reduction period of a claimant aged 16 or 17` `my age on the date of the failure` `the date of the failure` `the days to the soonest event` `my earlier failures`
    WHERE
        `the days to the soonest event` MEANS
            `reg 104(2)(a) — the number of days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with whichever event is soonest` `the date of the failure` `the date I met a compliance condition` `the date I fell within section 19` `the date I stopped being required to take a work preparation action` `the date my award ended`
        `my earlier failures` MEANS
            IF `I have an earlier failure of the same kind`
            THEN LIST (`Previous sanctionable failure` WITH
                `date of the previous sanctionable failure` IS `the date of that earlier failure`
                `reduction period applicable to the previous sanctionable failure, in days` IS `the reduction period that applied to that earlier failure in days`
                -- Placeholders: regulation 104 reads only the date, the reduction period and whether the failure falls within regulation 104(1).
                `the previous sanctionable failure was a pre-claim failure` IS FALSE
                `the previous sanctionable failure gave rise to a higher-level sanction` IS FALSE
                `the previous sanctionable failure falls within regulation 103(1)` IS FALSE
                `the previous sanctionable failure falls within regulation 104(1)` IS TRUE)
            ELSE EMPTY

-- Regulation 105. Lowest-level sanction: for a failure under section 27 by a claimant within section 20 of the Act to comply with a
-- requirement under that section, the reduction lasts until the day before the claimant meets a compliance condition, the day before they
-- fall within section 19, or the day the award ends, whichever is soonest.
@export How many days is my reduction period for a lowest-level failure (reg 105)?
GIVEN `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the failure one that is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act?
      `the work-related group I am in` IS A `Work-related group` @desc Which group are you in: no work-related requirements, work-focused interview only, work preparation, or all work-related requirements?
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a requirement under section 20 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a failure to comply with a requirement under section 20 of the Act?
      `the date of the failure` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the failure?
      `the date I met a compliance condition` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did you meet a compliance condition set by the Secretary of State? (leave blank if you have not)
      `the date I fell within section 19` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did you fall within section 19 of the Act? (leave blank if you have not)
      `the date my award ended` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did your award end, other than by your ceasing to be or becoming a member of a couple? (leave blank if it has not)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days is my reduction period for a lowest-level failure` IS
    IF `reg 105(1) — this regulation specifies the reduction period for the failure` `the failure is sanctionable under section 27 of the Act` `the work-related group I am in` `the failure is a failure to comply with a requirement under section 20 of the Act`
    THEN `reg 105(2) — the number of days beginning with the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with whichever event is soonest` `the date of the failure` `the date I met a compliance condition` `the date I fell within section 19` `the date my award ended`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `When my reduction starts, stops, and how much it is`

-- Regulation 106. A reduction period takes effect from the first day of the assessment period in which the Secretary of State decides to
-- reduce the award, or the first day of the next if the award is not reduced in that period, or if the award is already reduced for an
-- earlier failure, the first day it is no longer so reduced.
@export From what day does my reduction take effect (reg 106)?
GIVEN `the first day of the assessment period in which the Secretary of State decides to reduce my award` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the assessment period in which the Secretary of State decided that your award is to be reduced?
      `my award is not reduced in that assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount of your award for that assessment period not reduced in that period?
      `the first day of the next assessment period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the next assessment period?
      `my award is already reduced for an earlier failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your award for that assessment period (or the next) already subject to a reduction because of an earlier sanctionable failure?
      `the first day my award is no longer reduced for the earlier failure` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc What is the first day on which your award is no longer subject to that earlier reduction? (leave blank if not known)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From what day does my reduction take effect` IS
    `reg 106 — the day from which the reduction period takes effect` `the first day of the assessment period in which the Secretary of State decides to reduce my award` `my award is not reduced in that assessment period` `the first day of the next assessment period` `my award is already reduced for an earlier failure` `the first day my award is no longer reduced for the earlier failure`

-- Regulation 107(1). If an award ends while days of a reduction remain, the period keeps running; if the claimant becomes entitled to a
-- new award before it runs out, the new award is reduced for the days that remain.
@export How many days of my earlier reduction remain for my new award (reg 107(1))?
GIVEN `the days left in my total outstanding reduction period when my award ended` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days were left in your total outstanding reduction period when your award ended?
      `the date my award ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your award end?
      `the date I became entitled to a new award` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you become entitled to a new award?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of my earlier reduction remain for my new award` IS
    `reg 107(1) — the remainder of the total outstanding reduction period when the new award begins` `the days left in my total outstanding reduction period when my award ended` `the date my award ended` `the date I became entitled to a new award`

-- Regulation 107(2). If an award ends before the Secretary of State decides the award is to be reduced for a failure, and the decision
-- is made after the claimant becomes entitled to a new award, the decision is treated as made on the day before the earlier award ended.
@export On what day is the decision to reduce my award treated as made after a new award starts (reg 107(2))?
GIVEN `my earlier award ended before the Secretary of State decided to reduce it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your earlier award end before the Secretary of State determined that its amount is to be reduced?
      `the decision was made after I became entitled to a new award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the determination made after you became entitled to a new award?
      `the date my earlier award ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your earlier award end?
      `the date the Secretary of State made the decision` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Secretary of State make the determination?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day is the decision to reduce my award treated as made after a new award starts` IS
    `reg 107(2) — the day on which the determination is treated as made` `my earlier award ended before the Secretary of State decided to reduce it` `the decision was made after I became entitled to a new award` `the date my earlier award ended` `the date the Secretary of State made the decision`

-- Regulation 108. A reduction is suspended for any period during which section 6B, 7 or 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 (a benefit
-- fraud penalty) applies to the award, and begins again the day after.
@export Is my reduction suspended on this day (reg 108)?
GIVEN `the first day a benefit fraud penalty period applies to my award` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did a period begin during which section 6B, 7 or 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 applies to your award? (leave blank if none)
      `the last day of that period` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day does that period end? (leave blank if it has not ended)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my reduction suspended on this day` IF
    `reg 108 — the reduction is suspended on the day` `the first day a benefit fraud penalty period applies to my award` `the last day of that period` `the day I am asking about`

-- Regulation 109(1). A reduction ends where, since the date of the failure, the claimant has been in paid work for at least six months
-- and their monthly earnings in each month reached the amount in regulation 109(1)(b): their individual threshold, or if none, 16 hours
-- at the minimum wage rate, or the apprentice's threshold.
@export Does my reduction end because I have done paid work for six months (reg 109(1))?
GIVEN `months of paid work since the failure` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of paid work have you done since the date of the most recent failure that gave rise to a reduction?
      `my monthly earnings in each of those months` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What were your monthly earnings in each of those months, in pounds? (none if none)
      `the group I would otherwise be in` IS A `Work-related group` @desc Apart from your earnings, which group would you be in: no work-related requirements, work-focused interview only, work preparation, or all work-related requirements?
      `the hourly rate for my age under the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hourly rate that applies to your age under regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds?
      `my expected hours a week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week are you expected to spend looking for work and being available for it (regulation 88)?
      `I am employed under a contract of apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed under a contract of apprenticeship?
      `the apprentice rate under regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rate specified in regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (the apprentice rate), in pounds? (0 if not applicable)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my reduction end because I have done paid work for six months` IF
    `reg 109(1) — the reduction is to be terminated` `months of paid work since the failure` `my monthly earnings in each of those months` `my individual threshold` `the hourly rate for my age under the National Minimum Wage Regulations` `I am employed under a contract of apprenticeship` `my expected hours a week` `the apprentice rate under regulation 4A(1)(d) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`
    WHERE
        `my individual threshold` MEANS `reg 90(2) — the individual threshold` `the group I would otherwise be in` `the hourly rate for my age under the National Minimum Wage Regulations` `my expected hours a week`

-- Regulation 109(2). The ending of a reduction has effect from the first day of the assessment period in which the six months are
-- complete (if that date is within a period of entitlement), or from the first day of the first assessment period of any later award.
@export From what day does the ending of my reduction take effect (reg 109(2))?
GIVEN `the date my six months were complete is within a period of entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the date on which you completed six months of paid work fall within a period of entitlement to universal credit?
      `the first day of the assessment period in which that date falls` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc What is the first day of the assessment period in which that date falls? (leave blank if not applicable)
      `the first day of the first assessment period of any later award` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc What is the first day of the first assessment period of any later award? (leave blank if not applicable)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From what day does the ending of my reduction take effect` IS
    `reg 109(2) — the day from which the termination of the reduction has effect` `the date my six months were complete is within a period of entitlement` `the first day of the assessment period in which that date falls` `the first day of the first assessment period of any later award`

-- Regulation 109(3). A claimant treated as having earned income under the minimum income floor (regulation 62) for an assessment period
-- is taken to have monthly earnings equal to their individual threshold for it.
@export What monthly earnings am I taken to have for the six-month test if I am treated as having earned income under the minimum income floor (reg 109(3))?
GIVEN `I am treated as having earned income under regulation 62 for the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated as having earned income in accordance with regulation 62 in respect of the assessment period?
      `my monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your monthly earnings for that assessment period, in pounds?
      `the group I would otherwise be in` IS A `Work-related group` @desc Apart from your earnings, which group would you be in: no work-related requirements, work-focused interview only, work preparation, or all work-related requirements?
      `the hourly rate for my age under the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hourly rate that applies to your age under regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations, in pounds?
      `my expected hours a week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week are you expected to spend looking for work and being available for it (regulation 88)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What monthly earnings am I taken to have for the six-month test if I am treated as having earned income under the minimum income floor` IS
    `reg 109(3) — the monthly earnings the claimant is taken to have` `I am treated as having earned income under regulation 62 for the assessment period` `my monthly earnings` `my individual threshold`
    WHERE
        `my individual threshold` MEANS `reg 90(2) — the individual threshold` `the group I would otherwise be in` `the hourly rate for my age under the National Minimum Wage Regulations` `my expected hours a week`

-- Regulation 110, Steps 1 to 3. For each assessment period the reduction is the number of days (the days in the period, or if fewer the
-- days left in the total outstanding reduction period, less days of suspension) multiplied by the daily reduction rate, but not more than
-- the standard allowance (or half of it where only one of joint claimants is affected).
@export How much is my award reduced for this assessment period (reg 110)?
GIVEN `days in the assessment period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are there in the assessment period?
      `days left in my total outstanding reduction period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are left in your total outstanding reduction period?
      `days in the assessment period for which my reduction is suspended` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days in the assessment period is your reduction suspended under regulation 108 (a benefit fraud penalty applies)?
      `I am aged 16 or 17 at the end of the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, are you aged 16 or 17?
      `I am the responsible carer of a child under 1 at the end of the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 19 of the Act as the responsible carer of a child under the age of 1?
      `I fall within section 19 by pregnancy, adoption or fostering a child under 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 89(1)(c), (d) or (f) (pregnant or recently confined, an adopter within 12 months, or the responsible foster parent of a child under 1)?
      `I fall within section 20 at the end of the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 20 of the Act (work-focused interview requirement only)?
      `I fall within section 19 by limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 19 of the Act by virtue of having limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `my standard allowance` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the standard allowance that applies to your award, in pounds a month?
      `we claim jointly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim universal credit jointly with your partner?
      `the reduction applies to only one of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim jointly, does the reduction apply to only one of you?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my award reduced for this assessment period` IS
    `reg 110 — the amount of the reduction for the assessment period` `days in the assessment period` `days left in my total outstanding reduction period` `days in the assessment period for which my reduction is suspended` `my daily reduction rate` `my standard allowance` `we claim jointly` `the reduction applies to only one of us`
    WHERE
        `my daily reduction rate` MEANS `reg 111 — the daily reduction rate applied to the claimant` `my position` `my standard allowance` `we claim jointly`
        `my position` MEANS `Position at the end of the assessment period` WITH
            `the claimant is aged 16 or 17` IS `I am aged 16 or 17 at the end of the assessment period`
            `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of subsection (2)(c) of that section (responsible carer for a child under the age of 1)` IS `I am the responsible carer of a child under 1 at the end of the assessment period`
            `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 89(1)(c), (d) or (f)` IS `I fall within section 19 by pregnancy, adoption or fostering a child under 1`
            `the claimant falls within section 20 of the Act` IS `I fall within section 20 at the end of the assessment period`
            `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of having limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS `I fall within section 19 by limited capability for work and work-related activity`

-- Regulation 110, Step 4. The amount of the award after the reduction is the amount after any benefit cap deduction (Part 7) less the
-- reduction; the text does not stop it falling below nothing.
@export What is my award after the reduction for this assessment period (reg 110, Step 4)?
GIVEN `my award for the assessment period after any benefit cap deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your award for the assessment period after any deduction under Part 7 (the benefit cap), in pounds?
      `days in the assessment period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are there in the assessment period?
      `days left in my total outstanding reduction period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are left in your total outstanding reduction period?
      `days in the assessment period for which my reduction is suspended` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days in the assessment period is your reduction suspended under regulation 108 (a benefit fraud penalty applies)?
      `I am aged 16 or 17 at the end of the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, are you aged 16 or 17?
      `I am the responsible carer of a child under 1 at the end of the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 19 of the Act as the responsible carer of a child under the age of 1?
      `I fall within section 19 by pregnancy, adoption or fostering a child under 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 89(1)(c), (d) or (f) (pregnant or recently confined, an adopter within 12 months, or the responsible foster parent of a child under 1)?
      `I fall within section 20 at the end of the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 20 of the Act (work-focused interview requirement only)?
      `I fall within section 19 by limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 19 of the Act by virtue of having limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `my standard allowance` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the standard allowance that applies to your award, in pounds a month?
      `we claim jointly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim universal credit jointly with your partner?
      `the reduction applies to only one of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim jointly, does the reduction apply to only one of you?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my award after the reduction for this assessment period` IS
    `reg 110 Step 4 — the amount of the award after the reduction` `my award for the assessment period after any benefit cap deduction` `my reduction`
    WHERE
        `my reduction` MEANS
            `reg 110 — the amount of the reduction for the assessment period` `days in the assessment period` `days left in my total outstanding reduction period` `days in the assessment period for which my reduction is suspended` `my daily reduction rate` `my standard allowance` `we claim jointly` `the reduction applies to only one of us`
        `my daily reduction rate` MEANS `reg 111 — the daily reduction rate applied to the claimant` `my position` `my standard allowance` `we claim jointly`
        `my position` MEANS `Position at the end of the assessment period` WITH
            `the claimant is aged 16 or 17` IS `I am aged 16 or 17 at the end of the assessment period`
            `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of subsection (2)(c) of that section (responsible carer for a child under the age of 1)` IS `I am the responsible carer of a child under 1 at the end of the assessment period`
            `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 89(1)(c), (d) or (f)` IS `I fall within section 19 by pregnancy, adoption or fostering a child under 1`
            `the claimant falls within section 20 of the Act` IS `I fall within section 20 at the end of the assessment period`
            `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of having limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS `I fall within section 19 by limited capability for work and work-related activity`

-- Regulation 111. The daily reduction rate is the standard allowance multiplied by 12 and divided by 365, rounded down to 10 pence; 40% of
-- that for a claimant aged 16 or 17, a responsible carer of a child under 1, a pregnant claimant, an adopter or foster parent of a child
-- under 1, or a claimant within section 20; nil for a claimant within section 19 by limited capability for work and work-related activity;
-- and half of it for each of joint claimants.
@export What is the daily rate at which my award is reduced (reg 111)?
GIVEN `I am aged 16 or 17 at the end of the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, are you aged 16 or 17?
      `I am the responsible carer of a child under 1 at the end of the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 19 of the Act as the responsible carer of a child under the age of 1?
      `I fall within section 19 by pregnancy, adoption or fostering a child under 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 89(1)(c), (d) or (f) (pregnant or recently confined, an adopter within 12 months, or the responsible foster parent of a child under 1)?
      `I fall within section 20 at the end of the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 20 of the Act (work-focused interview requirement only)?
      `I fall within section 19 by limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 19 of the Act by virtue of having limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `my standard allowance` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the standard allowance that applies to your award, in pounds a month?
      `we claim jointly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim universal credit jointly with your partner?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the daily rate at which my award is reduced` IS
    `reg 111 — the daily reduction rate applied to the claimant` `my position` `my standard allowance` `we claim jointly`
    WHERE
        `my position` MEANS `Position at the end of the assessment period` WITH
            `the claimant is aged 16 or 17` IS `I am aged 16 or 17 at the end of the assessment period`
            `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of subsection (2)(c) of that section (responsible carer for a child under the age of 1)` IS `I am the responsible carer of a child under 1 at the end of the assessment period`
            `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 89(1)(c), (d) or (f)` IS `I fall within section 19 by pregnancy, adoption or fostering a child under 1`
            `the claimant falls within section 20 of the Act` IS `I fall within section 20 at the end of the assessment period`
            `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of having limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS `I fall within section 19 by limited capability for work and work-related activity`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Reductions that are not made, and benefit sanctions carried over`

-- Regulation 112. Schedule 11 has effect for a person who is or has been entitled to an employment and support allowance or a jobseeker's
-- allowance and who is or becomes entitled to universal credit.
@export Does Schedule 11 carry an earlier benefit sanction over to my universal credit (reg 112)?
GIVEN `I am or have been entitled to an employment and support allowance or a jobseeker's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or have you been, entitled to an employment and support allowance or a jobseeker's allowance?
      `I am or become entitled to universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or do you become, entitled to universal credit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Schedule 11 carry an earlier benefit sanction over to my universal credit` IF
    `reg 112 — Schedule 11 has effect in relation to the person` `I am or have been entitled to an employment and support allowance or a jobseeker's allowance` `I am or become entitled to universal credit`

-- Regulation 113(1). No reduction is made for a failure in any of seven cases: (a) a vacancy because of a strike; (b) ceasing paid work
-- or losing pay within a trial period (where the requirements were limited); (c) ceasing paid work or losing pay because of a strike;
-- (d) ceasing paid work in the regular or reserve forces; (e) a pre-claim failure whose reduction is used up by the days before the claim;
-- (f) ceasing paid work in a redundancy or lay-off; (g) misconduct or leaving without good reason, where earnings have not fallen below
-- the regulation 99(6) amount.
@export Will my award be left unreduced for this failure (reg 113(1))?
GIVEN `the failure is failing to apply for a vacancy or to take up an offer of paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the failure one listed in section 26(2)(b) or (c) of the Act (failure to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work, or to take up an offer of paid work)?
      `the vacancy is because of a strike arising from a trade dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the vacancy because of a strike arising from a trade dispute?
      `the failure is ceasing paid work or losing pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the failure one listed in section 26(2)(d) of the Act (you cease paid work or lose pay)?
      `my requirements are limited to a certain number of hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your work search and work availability requirements subject to limitations under sections 17(4) and 18(3) in respect of work available for a certain number of hours?
      `I took up paid work or more paid work for more hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take up paid work, or (being in paid work) take up more paid work for a greater number of hours?
      `I voluntarily ceased that work or lost pay within a trial period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you voluntarily cease that paid work, or more paid work, or lose pay, within a trial period?
      `I voluntarily ceased paid work or lost pay because of a strike` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you voluntarily cease paid work, or lose pay, because of a strike arising from a trade dispute?
      `I voluntarily ceased paid work in the forces or lost pay in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you voluntarily cease paid work as a member of the regular or reserve forces, or lose pay in that capacity?
      `the failure is a pre-claim failure under section 26(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the failure one listed in section 26(4) of the Act (before you claimed)?
      `the reduction period that would otherwise apply under regulation 102(4)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc How many days would the reduction period otherwise be under regulation 102(4)? (leave blank if there is none)
      `the date of the failure` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the failure?
      `the date of my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you claim universal credit?
      `I voluntarily ceased paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you voluntarily cease paid work?
      `I was dismissed for redundancy after volunteering or agreeing to be dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dismissed because of redundancy after volunteering or agreeing to be dismissed?
      `I ceased work on an agreed date under a voluntary redundancy agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease work on an agreed date, without being dismissed, in pursuance of an agreement relating to voluntary redundancy?
      `I was laid off or kept on short-time as section 148 of the Employment Rights Act 1996 describes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you laid off or kept on short-time to the extent specified in section 148 of the Employment Rights Act 1996, and did you comply with the requirements of that section?
      `the failure is misconduct or leaving paid work for no good reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason, cease paid work or lose pay?
      `how I claim` IS A `Claim basis` @desc Do you claim as a single claimant, as joint claimants, or as a single claimant who is a member of a couple?
      `my monthly earnings after the failure` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your monthly earnings after the failure, in pounds (your joint monthly earnings if you are a member of a couple)?
      `the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hourly rate specified in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (the adult rate), in pounds?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my award be left unreduced for this failure` IF
    `reg 113(1) — no reduction is made for the failure` `case a` `case b` `case c` `case d` `case e` `case f` `case g`
    WHERE
        `case a` MEANS `reg 113(1)(a) — no reduction: a vacancy because of a strike` `the failure is failing to apply for a vacancy or to take up an offer of paid work` `the vacancy is because of a strike arising from a trade dispute`
        `case b` MEANS `reg 113(1)(b) — no reduction: ceasing paid work or losing pay within a trial period` `the failure is ceasing paid work or losing pay` `my requirements are limited to a certain number of hours` `I took up paid work or more paid work for more hours` `I voluntarily ceased that work or lost pay within a trial period`
        `case c` MEANS `reg 113(1)(c) — no reduction: ceasing paid work or losing pay because of a strike` `I voluntarily ceased paid work or lost pay because of a strike`
        `case d` MEANS `reg 113(1)(d) — no reduction: ceasing paid work in the regular or reserve forces` `I voluntarily ceased paid work in the forces or lost pay in that capacity`
        `case e` MEANS `reg 113(1)(e) — no reduction: a pre-claim failure whose reduction is used up by the days before the claim` `the failure is a pre-claim failure under section 26(4)` `the reduction period that would otherwise apply under regulation 102(4)` `the date of the failure` `the date of my claim`
        `case f` MEANS `reg 113(1)(f) — no reduction: ceasing paid work in a redundancy or lay-off` `I voluntarily ceased paid work` `I was dismissed for redundancy after volunteering or agreeing to be dismissed` `I ceased work on an agreed date under a voluntary redundancy agreement` `I was laid off or kept on short-time as section 148 of the Employment Rights Act 1996 describes`
        `case g` MEANS `reg 113(1)(g) — no reduction: earnings have not fallen below the amount in regulation 99(6)` `the failure is misconduct or leaving paid work for no good reason` `how I claim` `my monthly earnings after the failure` `the hourly rate in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`

-- Regulation 114. A placement on the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme is a prescribed placement for section 26(2)(a) of the Act (failure to
-- participate in a prescribed employment scheme). The scheme is one provided under arrangements made by the Secretary of State, known by
-- that name, designed to provide work or work-related activity for up to 30 hours a week over up to 4 consecutive weeks, to help
-- claimants improve their prospects of employment.
@export Is my placement one that can lead to a reduction if I fail to take part in it (reg 114)?
GIVEN `I am placed on a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been placed on a scheme?
      `the scheme is provided under arrangements made by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme provided pursuant to arrangements made by the Secretary of State?
      `the scheme is called the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme known by the name Mandatory Work Activity Scheme?
      `the most hours a week the scheme is designed to provide` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the most hours a week of work or work-related activity that the scheme is designed to provide?
      `the number of consecutive weeks the scheme is designed to last` IS A NUMBER @desc Over how many consecutive weeks is the scheme designed to provide it?
      `the scheme is designed to improve my prospects of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme designed with a view to assisting claimants to improve their prospects of obtaining employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my placement one that can lead to a reduction if I fail to take part in it` IF
    `reg 114(1) — the placement is a prescribed placement for section 26(2)(a) of the Act` `I am placed on a scheme` `the scheme is the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme`
    WHERE
        `the scheme is the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme` MEANS
            `reg 114(2) — the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme` `the scheme is provided under arrangements made by the Secretary of State` `the scheme is called the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme` `the most hours a week the scheme is designed to provide` `the number of consecutive weeks the scheme is designed to last` `the scheme is designed to improve my prospects of employment`

-- Schedule 11, paragraph 1. If a person was entitled to an employment and support allowance, had its amount reduced under section 11J of
-- the Welfare Reform Act 2007, and becomes entitled to universal credit, the reduction is applied to the universal credit award for the
-- days that remain of the period under regulations 52 and 53 of the ESA Regulations. The answer is NOTHING when paragraph 1 does not apply.
@export How many days of an employment and support allowance sanction are carried over to my universal credit (Schedule 11 para 1)?
GIVEN `I am or have ceased to be entitled to an employment and support allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or have you ceased to be, entitled to an employment and support allowance?
      `my employment and support allowance was reduced under section 11J of the Welfare Reform Act 2007` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a reduction relating to your employment and support allowance under section 11J of the Welfare Reform Act 2007?
      `I become entitled to universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you become entitled to universal credit?
      `days that applied to me under regulations 52 and 53 of the ESA Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days applied to you under regulations 52 and 53 of the ESA Regulations?
      `days that have already reduced my employment and support allowance` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those days have already resulted in a reduction to the amount of your employment and support allowance?
      `the date my employment and support allowance ended` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did your award of employment and support allowance end? (leave blank if it has not)
      `the date my universal credit starts` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your award of universal credit start?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of an employment and support allowance sanction are carried over to my universal credit` IS
    IF `Sch 11 para 1(2) — the reduction is applied to the award of universal credit` (`Sch 11 para 1(1) — this paragraph applies` `I am or have ceased to be entitled to an employment and support allowance` `my employment and support allowance was reduced under section 11J of the Welfare Reform Act 2007` `I become entitled to universal credit`)
    THEN JUST (`Sch 11 para 1(3) — the period for which the reduction is to have effect` `days that applied to me under regulations 52 and 53 of the ESA Regulations` `days that have already reduced my employment and support allowance` `the date my employment and support allowance ended` `the date my universal credit starts`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Schedule 11, paragraph 2. The same for a jobseeker's allowance reduced under section 6J or 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995, for the days
-- that remain of the period under regulations 19 to 21 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 2013.
@export How many days of a jobseeker's allowance sanction are carried over to my universal credit (Schedule 11 para 2)?
GIVEN `I am or have ceased to be entitled to a jobseeker's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or have you ceased to be, entitled to a jobseeker's allowance?
      `my jobseeker's allowance was reduced under section 6J or 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a reduction relating to your jobseeker's allowance under section 6J or 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995?
      `I become entitled to universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you become entitled to universal credit?
      `days that applied to me under regulations 19 to 21 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 2013` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days applied to you under regulations 19 to 21 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 2013?
      `days that have already reduced my jobseeker's allowance` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those days have already resulted in a reduction to the amount of your jobseeker's allowance?
      `the date my jobseeker's allowance ended` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did your award of jobseeker's allowance end? (leave blank if it has not)
      `the date my universal credit starts` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your award of universal credit start?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of a jobseeker's allowance sanction are carried over to my universal credit` IS
    IF `Sch 11 para 2(2) — the reduction is applied to the award of universal credit` (`Sch 11 para 2(1) — this paragraph applies` `I am or have ceased to be entitled to a jobseeker's allowance` `my jobseeker's allowance was reduced under section 6J or 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995` `I become entitled to universal credit`)
    THEN JUST (`Sch 11 para 2(3) — the period for which the reduction is to have effect` `days that applied to me under regulations 19 to 21 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 2013` `days that have already reduced my jobseeker's allowance` `the date my jobseeker's allowance ended` `the date my universal credit starts`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Schedule 11, paragraph 3. Where a reduction for an employment and support allowance or a jobseeker's allowance is applied to an award of
-- universal credit and the claimant later has a sanctionable failure under section 26 or 27, the earlier failure and its period are treated
-- as the corresponding failure and reduction period for the reduction-period tables, if they correspond with a failure specified under
-- section 26 or 27 to which the same period applies.
@export Is my earlier employment and support allowance or jobseeker's allowance failure counted as an earlier failure for my universal credit (Schedule 11 para 3)?
GIVEN `a reduction for my earlier benefit has been applied to my universal credit under Schedule 11` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a reduction relating to your award of employment and support allowance or jobseeker's allowance been applied to your award of universal credit under paragraph 1 or 2 of Schedule 11?
      `I now have a sanctionable failure under section 26 or 27` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you now have a sanctionable failure under section 26 or 27 of the Act?
      `the earlier failure and its period correspond with a failure under section 26 or 27` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the earlier failure and the reduction period determined for it correspond with a failure specified under section 26 or 27 of the Act to which the same reduction period applies?
      `the date of that earlier failure` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the earlier failure?
      `the reduction period that applied to that earlier failure in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days was the reduction period for that earlier failure?
      `that earlier failure was a pre-claim failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that earlier failure a pre-claim failure?
      `that earlier failure gave rise to a higher-level sanction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that earlier failure give rise to a higher-level sanction?
      `that earlier failure falls within regulation 103(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that earlier failure fall within regulation 103(1) (a work search requirement under section 17(1)(a) or a work availability requirement)?
      `that earlier failure falls within regulation 104(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that earlier failure fall within regulation 104(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my earlier employment and support allowance or jobseeker's allowance failure counted as an earlier failure for my universal credit` IF
    CONSIDER `Sch 11 para 3 — the previous failure is treated as the corresponding failure` `a reduction for my earlier benefit has been applied to my universal credit under Schedule 11` `I now have a sanctionable failure under section 26 or 27` `the earlier failure and its period correspond with a failure under section 26 or 27` `my earlier failure`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST counted THEN TRUE
    WHERE
        `my earlier failure` MEANS `Previous sanctionable failure` WITH
            `date of the previous sanctionable failure` IS `the date of that earlier failure`
            `reduction period applicable to the previous sanctionable failure, in days` IS `the reduction period that applied to that earlier failure in days`
            `the previous sanctionable failure was a pre-claim failure` IS `that earlier failure was a pre-claim failure`
            `the previous sanctionable failure gave rise to a higher-level sanction` IS `that earlier failure gave rise to a higher-level sanction`
            `the previous sanctionable failure falls within regulation 103(1)` IS `that earlier failure falls within regulation 103(1)`
            `the previous sanctionable failure falls within regulation 104(1)` IS `that earlier failure falls within regulation 104(1)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Hardship payments`
-- Only for a person whose award has been reduced for a failure; the form should ask "Has your award been reduced?" first.

-- Regulation 116(1) to (3). A hardship payment is made only where the claimant whose award was reduced is 18 or over; the claimant (each
-- joint claimant) has met any compliance condition; completes and submits an application in the form and manner the Secretary of State
-- accepts or determines, and furnishes any information or evidence required; accepts that hardship payments are recoverable; the
-- Secretary of State is satisfied that each complied with all work-related requirements in the 7 days before the application and is
-- in hardship (cannot meet their, or a child's, immediate and most basic needs of accommodation, heating, food or hygiene only because of
-- the reduction, and has made every effort to find other support and to stop other spending); and the daily reduction rate in
-- regulation 111(1) applies (not the 40% or nil rates).
@export Can I get a hardship payment (reg 116)?
GIVEN `the age of the claimant whose award was reduced` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the claimant in respect of whose failure the award was reduced?
      `I have met any compliance condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you met any compliance condition the Secretary of State specified under regulation 104(2)(a)(i)?
      `I completed and submitted an application in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you complete and submit an application in the form the Secretary of State approved, or in another form they accept as sufficient?
      `I completed and submitted it in the manner determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you complete and submit the application in the manner the Secretary of State determines?
      `I gave the information or evidence required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you furnish the information or evidence the Secretary of State required, in the manner they determine?
      `I accept that hardship payments are recoverable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you accept that any hardship payments that are paid are recoverable?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied I complied with my work-related requirements in the 7 days before applying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that you complied with all the work-related requirements you were required to comply with in the 7 days before the day you applied?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied I am in hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied that you are in hardship?
      `we claim jointly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim universal credit jointly with your partner?
      `my partner has met any compliance condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim jointly, has your partner met any compliance condition the Secretary of State specified under regulation 104(2)(a)(i)? (no if not applicable)
      `my partner completed and submitted an application in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim jointly, did your partner complete and submit an application in the approved form? (no if not applicable)
      `my partner completed and submitted it in the manner determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim jointly, did your partner complete and submit it in the manner determined? (no if not applicable)
      `my partner gave the information or evidence required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim jointly, did your partner furnish the information or evidence required? (no if not applicable)
      `my partner accepts that hardship payments are recoverable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim jointly, does your partner accept that hardship payments are recoverable? (no if not applicable)
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied my partner complied with their work-related requirements in the 7 days before applying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim jointly, has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied your partner complied with all their work-related requirements in the 7 days before applying? (no if not applicable)
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied my partner is in hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim jointly, has the Secretary of State said they are satisfied your partner is in hardship? (no if not applicable)
      `needs we cannot meet only because of the reduction` IS A LIST OF `Essential need` @desc Which of these needs can you not meet only because your award has been reduced? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `needs of a child I am responsible for that cannot be met only because of the reduction` IS A LIST OF `Essential need` @desc Which of these needs of a child or qualifying young person you are responsible for can you not meet only because your award has been reduced? Choose all that apply, or none.
      `the reduction is at the daily rate in regulation 111(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reduction by the daily reduction rate in regulation 111(1) under section 26 or 27 of the Act?
      `the reduction is at the equivalent rate under the Social Security Fraud Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reduction by the equivalent daily reduction rate prescribed under section 6B(5A), 7(2A) or 9(2A) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001?
      `we have made every effort to find other support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made every effort to access alternative sources of support to meet, or partially meet, those needs?
      `we have made every effort to cut other spending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made every effort to cease to incur any expenditure that does not relate to those needs?
      `I am aged 16 or 17 at the end of the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, are you aged 16 or 17?
      `I am the responsible carer of a child under 1 at the end of the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 19 of the Act as the responsible carer of a child under the age of 1?
      `I fall within section 19 by pregnancy, adoption or fostering a child under 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 89(1)(c), (d) or (f) (pregnant or recently confined, an adopter within 12 months, or the responsible foster parent of a child under 1)?
      `I fall within section 20 at the end of the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 20 of the Act (work-focused interview requirement only)?
      `I fall within section 19 by limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the assessment period, do you fall within section 19 of the Act by virtue of having limited capability for work and work-related activity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I get a hardship payment` IF
    `reg 116(1) — the conditions for a hardship payment are met` `limb a` `limb b` `limb c` `limb d` `limb e` `limb f` `limb g` `limb h`
    WHERE
        `limb a` MEANS `reg 116(1)(a) — the sanctioned claimant is aged 18 or over` `the age of the claimant whose award was reduced`
        `limb b` MEANS `reg 116(1)(b) — each claimant has met any compliance condition` `the claimants`
        `limb c` MEANS `reg 116(1)(c) — a claimant completes and submits an application` `the claimants`
        `limb d` MEANS `reg 116(1)(d) — a claimant furnishes the information or evidence required` `the claimants`
        `limb e` MEANS `reg 116(1)(e) — each claimant accepts that hardship payments are recoverable` `the claimants`
        `limb f` MEANS `reg 116(1)(f) — each claimant has complied with the work-related requirements in the 7 days before the application` `the claimants`
        `limb g` MEANS `reg 116(1)(g) — each claimant is in hardship` `the claimants` (`reg 116(2) — the claimants are in hardship` `our hardship facts`)
        `limb h` MEANS `reg 116(1)(h) — the daily reduction rate in regulation 111(1) applies` `my position`
        `the claimants` MEANS
            IF `we claim jointly`
            THEN LIST `my conditions`, `my partner's conditions`
            ELSE LIST `my conditions`
        `my conditions` MEANS `Hardship conditions of one claimant` WITH
            `has met any compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State under regulation 104(2)(a)(i)` IS `I have met any compliance condition`
            `completes and submits an application approved for the purpose by the Secretary of State, or in such other form as the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient` IS `I completed and submitted an application in the approved form`
            `completes and submits the application in such manner as the Secretary of State determines` IS `I completed and submitted it in the manner determined`
            `furnishes such information or evidence as the Secretary of State may require, in such manner as the Secretary of State determines` IS `I gave the information or evidence required`
            `accepts that any hardship payments that are paid are recoverable` IS `I accept that hardship payments are recoverable`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant has complied with all the work-related requirements that they were required to comply with in the 7 days preceding the day on which the application was submitted` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied I complied with my work-related requirements in the 7 days before applying`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant is in hardship` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied I am in hardship`
        `my partner's conditions` MEANS `Hardship conditions of one claimant` WITH
            `has met any compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State under regulation 104(2)(a)(i)` IS `my partner has met any compliance condition`
            `completes and submits an application approved for the purpose by the Secretary of State, or in such other form as the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient` IS `my partner completed and submitted an application in the approved form`
            `completes and submits the application in such manner as the Secretary of State determines` IS `my partner completed and submitted it in the manner determined`
            `furnishes such information or evidence as the Secretary of State may require, in such manner as the Secretary of State determines` IS `my partner gave the information or evidence required`
            `accepts that any hardship payments that are paid are recoverable` IS `my partner accepts that hardship payments are recoverable`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant has complied with all the work-related requirements that they were required to comply with in the 7 days preceding the day on which the application was submitted` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied my partner complied with their work-related requirements in the 7 days before applying`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant is in hardship` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied my partner is in hardship`
        `our hardship facts` MEANS `Facts for hardship` WITH
            `essential needs that the claimants cannot meet only because the amount of their award has been reduced` IS `needs we cannot meet only because of the reduction`
            `essential needs of a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible that cannot be met only because the amount of the award has been reduced` IS `needs of a child I am responsible for that cannot be met only because of the reduction`
            `the reduction is by the daily reduction rate set out in regulation 111(1) under section 26 or 27 of the Act` IS `the reduction is at the daily rate in regulation 111(1)`
            `the reduction is by the equivalent daily reduction rate prescribed in regulations made under section 6B(5A), 7(2A) or 9(2A) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001` IS `the reduction is at the equivalent rate under the Social Security Fraud Act 2001`
            `they have made every effort to access alternative sources of support to meet, or partially meet, such needs` IS `we have made every effort to find other support`
            `they have made every effort to cease to incur any expenditure which does not relate to such needs` IS `we have made every effort to cut other spending`
        `my position` MEANS `Position at the end of the assessment period` WITH
            `the claimant is aged 16 or 17` IS `I am aged 16 or 17 at the end of the assessment period`
            `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of subsection (2)(c) of that section (responsible carer for a child under the age of 1)` IS `I am the responsible carer of a child under 1 at the end of the assessment period`
            `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 89(1)(c), (d) or (f)` IS `I fall within section 19 by pregnancy, adoption or fostering a child under 1`
            `the claimant falls within section 20 of the Act` IS `I fall within section 20 at the end of the assessment period`
            `the claimant falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of having limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS `I fall within section 19 by limited capability for work and work-related activity`

-- Regulation 117. A hardship payment is made for a period beginning on the date all the regulation 116(1) conditions are met and ending
-- the day before the normal payment date for that assessment period; but if that period would be 7 days or less (both ends counted)
-- it ends on the normal payment date for the following assessment period or, if earlier, the last day on which the award is reduced.
@export Until what day will my hardship payment run (reg 117)?
GIVEN `the date all my hardship conditions are met` IS A DATE @desc On what date were all the conditions for a hardship payment met?
      `the normal payment date for that assessment period` IS A DATE @desc What is the normal payment date for the assessment period in which they were met?
      `the normal payment date for the following assessment period` IS A DATE @desc What is the normal payment date for the following assessment period?
      `the last day on which my award is reduced` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc What is the last day on which your award is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act, or under section 6B(5A), 7(2A) or 9(2A) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001? (leave blank if not known)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until what day will my hardship payment run` IS
    (`reg 117 — the period in respect of which a hardship payment is made` `the date all my hardship conditions are met` `the normal payment date for that assessment period` `the normal payment date for the following assessment period` `the last day on which my award is reduced`)'s `last day of the period`

-- Regulation 118. The hardship payment for each day is 60% of the amount of the reduction in the award calculated under regulation 110 for
-- the assessment period before the one in which the application is made, multiplied by 12 and divided by 365 (to the nearest penny).
@export How much is my hardship payment for each day (reg 118)?
GIVEN `the amount of my reduction for the assessment period before I applied` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the amount of the reduction in your award, calculated under regulation 110, for the assessment period before the one in which you applied for a hardship payment, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my hardship payment for each day` IS
    `reg 118 — the amount of a hardship payment for each day` `the amount of my reduction for the assessment period before I applied`

-- Regulation 119. Hardship payments are recoverable, except in an assessment period in which the claimant (each joint claimant) falls within
-- section 19 by regulation 90, or their earnings reach the individual threshold (where it applies to one joint claimant only) or the amount
-- for 16 hours a week at the minimum wage rate for their age (where it applies to neither); and the duty to repay stops once, since the
-- reduction last applied, such assessment periods have totalled six months.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Facts for the recoverability of hardship payments`
`seat — a list of n assessment periods in each of which regulation 119(2)(a) is met` n MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE (`Facts for the recoverability of hardship payments` WITH
              `the single claimant, or each joint claimant, falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90` IS TRUE
              `regulation 90 applies to one of the joint claimants only` IS FALSE
              `regulation 90 applies to neither the single claimant nor either joint claimant` IS FALSE
              `the single claimant's monthly earnings, or the joint claimants' combined monthly earnings` IS 0
              `the amount of the individual threshold` IS NOTHING
              `the hourly rate in regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for a person of the same age as the claimant, or the youngest of the joint claimants` IS 0)
         FOLLOWED BY (`seat — a list of n assessment periods in each of which regulation 119(2)(a) is met` (n MINUS 1))

@export Must I repay hardship payments for this assessment period (reg 119)?
GIVEN `I (or each of us) fall within section 19 by virtue of regulation 90` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you (or each of you, if you claim jointly) fall within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90?
      `regulation 90 applies to only one of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim jointly, does regulation 90 apply to only one of you?
      `regulation 90 applies to neither of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 90 apply to neither you nor your partner?
      `my monthly earnings, or our combined monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your monthly earnings (or your combined monthly earnings, if you claim jointly), in pounds?
      `my individual threshold` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc What is your individual threshold under regulation 90 (the amount for 16 hours a week, or for your expected hours), in pounds? (leave blank if you have none)
      `the hourly rate for my age under the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hourly rate under regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for a person of your age (or the youngest of you, if you claim jointly), in pounds?
      `earlier assessment periods since my reduction last applied in which I met regulation 119(2)` IS A NUMBER @desc Since the last day your award was subject to a reduction, in how many earlier assessment periods have you met paragraph (2)(a), (b) or (c) of regulation 119?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I repay hardship payments for this assessment period` IF
    `reg 119(1) — hardship payments are recoverable` `paragraph (2) applies` `paragraph (3) has ended it`
    WHERE
        `paragraph (2) applies` MEANS `reg 119(2) — the assessment period is outside the recovery of paragraph (1)` `this assessment period`
        `paragraph (3) has ended it` MEANS `reg 119(3) — paragraph (1) has ceased to apply` (`this assessment period` FOLLOWED BY (`seat — a list of n assessment periods in each of which regulation 119(2)(a) is met` `earlier assessment periods since my reduction last applied in which I met regulation 119(2)`))
        `this assessment period` MEANS `Facts for the recoverability of hardship payments` WITH
            `the single claimant, or each joint claimant, falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90` IS `I (or each of us) fall within section 19 by virtue of regulation 90`
            `regulation 90 applies to one of the joint claimants only` IS `regulation 90 applies to only one of us`
            `regulation 90 applies to neither the single claimant nor either joint claimant` IS `regulation 90 applies to neither of us`
            `the single claimant's monthly earnings, or the joint claimants' combined monthly earnings` IS `my monthly earnings, or our combined monthly earnings`
            `the amount of the individual threshold` IS `my individual threshold`
            `the hourly rate in regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for a person of the same age as the claimant, or the youngest of the joint claimants` IS `the hourly rate for my age under the National Minimum Wage Regulations`
